asr-000400
00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:22.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We also need to understand how learning recovery interventions will reach the children who need them the most.

asr-000401
00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:26.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But we should also recognize the progress that has been made.

asr-000402
00:42:26.840 --> 00:42:33.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The Philippines' improved performance in the 2025 Program for International Student Assessment, or PISA,

asr-000403
00:42:34.780 --> 00:42:38.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: with gains in reading, mathematics, and science is an encouraging development.

asr-000404
00:42:38.720 --> 00:42:41.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Saludo tayo sa Department of Education.

asr-000405
00:42:41.560 --> 00:42:42.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siyempre sa atin.

asr-000406
00:42:42.020 --> 00:42:49.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa ating Secretary Angara, sa ating maguro at school leaders, at sa ating mga learners dahil sa tagumpay na ito.

asr-000407
00:42:49.680 --> 00:42:54.580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa kabila ng mga hamon sa ating sistema na edukasyon, may pag-usad tayong nakikita.

asr-000408
00:42:55.080 --> 00:42:58.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ngayon pa man, maraming pa tayong kailangan gawin at pagbutihin.

asr-000409
00:42:58.640 --> 00:43:02.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In the past few days, since the Senate received the General Appropriations Bill,

asr-000410
00:43:02.860 --> 00:43:08.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: we've observed that the House version introduces steep adjustments to the proposed budget,

asr-000411
00:43:09.280 --> 00:43:11.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: including reductions in computerization,

asr-000412
00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:17.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: basic education facilities, teacher development, and foreign-assisted projects.

asr-000413
00:43:18.040 --> 00:43:20.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: This morning, that's what we want to find out.

asr-000414
00:43:20.700 --> 00:43:22.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga tayo nagkaroon ng budgeteering.

asr-000415
00:43:22.900 --> 00:43:27.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, we would like to hear from Secretary Angara and the Department

asr-000416
00:43:27.220 --> 00:43:37.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ano po ang magiging epekto nitong mga pagbawas na ito sa ating programa, main program, sa ating DepEd.

asr-000417
00:43:37.220 --> 00:43:42.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga po, kung kinakailangan talaga, ay gagawan nating paraan.

asr-000418
00:43:42.940 --> 00:43:48.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: nung isang taon, we are quite proud that in spite of the floodgate scandal,

asr-000419
00:43:49.080 --> 00:43:53.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: the reforms that were started here in the Senate by then Finance Chair,

asr-000420
00:43:53.860 --> 00:43:58.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Gatchal Yan, gave focus and priority to the Department of Education.

asr-000421
00:43:59.100 --> 00:44:05.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga, ang ganda ho, tignan, that DepEd was at the center, talagang pinakamalaking budget.

asr-000422
00:44:05.280 --> 00:44:10.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga, ang pagbawas ng 6 billion sa HGAB,

asr-000423
00:44:12.020 --> 00:44:14.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ang bubusisiin sa umagang ito.

asr-000424
00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:19.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We must understand what these changes mean on the ground,

asr-000425
00:44:19.160 --> 00:44:21.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which schools and learners will be affected,

asr-000426
00:44:21.620 --> 00:44:23.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: which commitments can still be delivered,

asr-000427
00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:26.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and where funding needs to be restored or increased,

asr-000428
00:44:27.200 --> 00:44:29.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and what concrete results can DepEd commit to.

asr-000429
00:44:30.340 --> 00:44:33.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: When we recognize the scale of the task before DepEd,

asr-000430
00:44:33.400 --> 00:44:37.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and the dedication of the teachers and persons who keep our schools running,

asr-000431
00:44:37.900 --> 00:44:41.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: sa huli, ang sukatan ng budget na ito ay makikita sa mismong karanasan,

asr-000432
00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:42.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ng ating mga siyudyante.

asr-000433
00:44:43.240 --> 00:44:46.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: May mga guro bang gumagabay, may kagamitang nagagamit,

asr-000434
00:44:46.940 --> 00:44:49.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: may ligtas at maayos pang lugar para sa mag-aaral,

asr-000435
00:44:49.700 --> 00:44:52.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: at may kaalamang bang nagdadagdag sa bawat taon.

asr-000436
00:44:53.340 --> 00:44:56.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Every peso invested in education must help make that possible.

asr-000437
00:44:57.660 --> 00:45:00.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: With that, I yield the floor to our...

asr-000438
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:07.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: subcommittee chair, of course, one of our strongest advocates for education here in the Senate,

asr-000439
00:45:07.880 --> 00:45:10.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: subcommittee chair, Senator Bam Aquino, to lead today's proceedings.

asr-000440
00:45:10.660 --> 00:45:11.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000441
00:45:11.940 --> 00:45:14.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Senator Gachalian.

asr-000442
00:45:14.680 --> 00:45:16.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And then we'll have Senator Cayetano.

asr-000443
00:45:16.600 --> 00:45:17.780
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000444
00:45:17.780 --> 00:45:25.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Mr. Chairman, I just want to show three slides dahil 2026 ay naging napaka-importante

asr-000445
00:45:25.740 --> 00:45:30.700
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: at maraming magagandang nangyari for 2026 in the education sector.

asr-000446
00:45:31.340 --> 00:45:36.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So first of all, nagkaroon po tayo ng isa sa pinakamataas na budget pagdating sa education sector,

asr-000447
00:45:37.420 --> 00:45:42.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: about 1.3 trillion pesos or about 4.36% of GDP.

asr-000448
00:45:42.500 --> 00:45:52.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So ito ay pasok na pasok na doon sa requirement ng international standards na 4 to 6% of GDP allocated to education.

asr-000449
00:45:52.780 --> 00:45:55.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pero alam ko marami rin challenges dahil isang...

asr-000450
00:45:55.740 --> 00:46:00.420
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Isa sa pinakamalaking challenges dito ay yung absorptive capacity,

asr-000451
00:46:00.620 --> 00:46:02.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: kung paano gastusin naman itong pondo na ito.

asr-000452
00:46:03.360 --> 00:46:05.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At yan ang pag-uusapan natin ngayong araw na ito.

asr-000453
00:46:05.460 --> 00:46:13.380
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Alam ko binabantayan ho ng ating chairman of the basic education, si Senator Bam Aquino,

asr-000454
00:46:13.900 --> 00:46:16.980
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: yung efficient na paggastos nitong budget na ito.

asr-000455
00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:23.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pangalawa, and I have to congratulate the Department of Education under the leadership of Senator Sani Angara,

asr-000456
00:46:24.220 --> 00:46:25.460
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: tayo ang most improved country.

asr-000457
00:46:25.740 --> 00:46:26.880
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: pagdating sa PISA.

asr-000458
00:46:27.460 --> 00:46:32.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At napakalaking bagay ito, both for the education sector and also for national pride.

asr-000459
00:46:33.400 --> 00:46:36.500
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil nung unang labas ng PISA, tayo pinakahuli.

asr-000460
00:46:37.020 --> 00:46:38.560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ngayon, hindi na tayo pinakahuli.

asr-000461
00:46:39.100 --> 00:46:39.960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Most improved pa.

asr-000462
00:46:40.280 --> 00:46:44.920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So we also want to understand from the Department of Education, yung gains.

asr-000463
00:46:45.680 --> 00:46:47.740
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And of course, how to sustain the gains.

asr-000464
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:53.220
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Sana tuloy-tuloy na ho ito pagdating ng mga susunod na panahon.

asr-000465
00:46:53.220 --> 00:46:55.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At lastly, on the local...

asr-000466
00:46:55.740 --> 00:47:03.840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: On the local front, yung aral program through the aral law, malaki rin ang improvements pagdating sa literacy.

asr-000467
00:47:04.380 --> 00:47:10.180
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 1.3 million students in grades 1 to 10 ang nag-improve.

asr-000468
00:47:10.840 --> 00:47:18.300
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dati problema natin yung pagbabasa at pagbibilang ngayon ay dahil dito sa aral program,

asr-000469
00:47:18.300 --> 00:47:25.240
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: ay malaki ang natulungan natin mga mag-aaral na magbasa sila at marunong magbilang.

asr-000470
00:47:25.740 --> 00:47:28.620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So we also want to understand how we can sustain this program.

asr-000471
00:47:29.500 --> 00:47:34.800
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Naintindihan ko na hindi nabigyan ng pondo ito this 2027.

asr-000472
00:47:35.720 --> 00:47:42.320
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: At yun naman ang aming magiging commitment sa Department of Education.

asr-000473
00:47:42.600 --> 00:47:49.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dahil kung maganda yung programa, dapat mapondohan para masustain yung gains nitong programa na ito.

asr-000474
00:47:49.040 --> 00:47:54.480
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So 2026 was a good year for the education sector.

asr-000475
00:47:54.620 --> 00:47:55.040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Marami tayong makikitang...

asr-000476
00:47:55.740 --> 00:47:57.200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Magagandang nangyayari.

asr-000477
00:47:57.760 --> 00:48:05.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ang next challenge natin is paano natin masustain itong mga naumpisahan na natin through the 2027 budget.

asr-000478
00:48:05.560 --> 00:48:10.060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So with that, I thank the Chairman of the Subcommittee on Education.

asr-000479
00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:11.000
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000480
00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:13.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Senator Gachalian, SP.

asr-000481
00:48:13.620 --> 00:48:14.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Senator Cayetano.

asr-000482
00:48:14.640 --> 00:48:21.220
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: Sir Chairman and Mr. Senate President, with your permission, may I yield because Senator Pia has another appointment.

asr-000483
00:48:21.220 --> 00:48:25.720
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: And since she formed part of my education, I will...

asr-000484
00:48:25.740 --> 00:48:28.740
Senator Alan Peter S. Cayetano: I will pass first the privilege to...

asr-000485
00:48:29.300 --> 00:48:30.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you.

asr-000486
00:48:30.140 --> 00:48:31.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Senator Pia is recognized.

asr-000487
00:48:31.920 --> 00:48:35.980
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Our colleagues know we have some important visitors that I have to attend to.

asr-000488
00:48:36.100 --> 00:48:36.880
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll make it very brief.

asr-000489
00:48:36.960 --> 00:48:41.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I just wanted to have the opportunity to greet our Secretary and the whole DepEd team.

asr-000490
00:48:41.440 --> 00:48:42.260
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I miss all of you.

asr-000491
00:48:42.320 --> 00:48:51.640
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: As you know, I defended the DepEd budget and all the attached agencies when the Secretary was our Chairman of the Committee on Finance.

asr-000492
00:48:51.640 --> 00:48:55.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So just very briefly, well, welcome.

asr-000493
00:48:55.420 --> 00:48:58.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: First of all, and of course, I always tie this into the SDGs, no?

asr-000494
00:48:58.980 --> 00:49:09.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The Chairman spoke lengthily about stunting and that ties into SDG 2 on zero hunger, SDG 3 on good health and well-being.

asr-000495
00:49:09.260 --> 00:49:12.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: A lot of our health programs are implemented through the schools.

asr-000496
00:49:12.560 --> 00:49:14.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: SDG 5 on gender equality.

asr-000497
00:49:14.640 --> 00:49:15.740
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: We still have...

asr-000498
00:49:15.740 --> 00:49:23.620
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: There's so much to say about gender equality, but my biggest issue is how girls are most affected by teen pregnancies.

asr-000499
00:49:23.620 --> 00:49:25.300
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Boys are not really...

asr-000500
00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:26.860
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: They're not really affected by teen pregnancies.

asr-000501
00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:28.920
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's the girls who are affected by teen pregnancies.

asr-000502
00:49:29.020 --> 00:49:30.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So we've got to work harder on that.

asr-000503
00:49:31.220 --> 00:49:35.180
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then SDG 8 on decent work and economic growth.

asr-000504
00:49:35.960 --> 00:49:40.420
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Of course, the foundation happens in basic education.

asr-000505
00:49:41.040 --> 00:49:46.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I'll add SDG 11 on safe, resilient, and sustainable cities and communities.

asr-000506
00:49:46.340 --> 00:49:51.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: As we talk about safeties in the schools, this really affects the entire environment, the entire communities.

asr-000507
00:49:53.040 --> 00:49:55.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So I also want to emphasize...

asr-000508
00:49:55.420 --> 00:50:03.660
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: On the importance of future-proofing our education, the Secretary and those colleagues of ours who've been around since 2019,

asr-000509
00:50:03.820 --> 00:50:06.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I've been harping on this for a long time.

asr-000510
00:50:06.160 --> 00:50:14.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So now, when I started talking about the future of education, having a futures-thinking mindset, it was kind of vague.

asr-000511
00:50:14.600 --> 00:50:18.460
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But now that AI is here, I think it's more...

asr-000512
00:50:18.460 --> 00:50:20.060
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: It's something easier for us to grasp.

asr-000513
00:50:20.060 --> 00:50:25.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And so the challenge is really how to use AI but not let it take over the lives of our children.

asr-000514
00:50:25.420 --> 00:50:32.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm not here to lecture, but I'm here to listen on how we are engaging with this new development,

asr-000515
00:50:33.060 --> 00:50:40.600
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: how we can maximize this as a tool for our teachers, for our tool for those who are working in terms of planning,

asr-000516
00:50:40.820 --> 00:50:43.560
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: the supervisors, the principals, and so on and so forth.

asr-000517
00:50:44.200 --> 00:50:50.500
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I also, again, again, since 2019, want to emphasize in as much as we want,

asr-000518
00:50:50.500 --> 00:50:55.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: we obviously want to see our children reading well and doing math.

asr-000519
00:50:55.420 --> 00:51:00.220
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: The four Cs, critical thinking, creativity, collaboration, communications.

asr-000520
00:51:02.280 --> 00:51:12.160
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I started speaking about this around 2019, but now with AI threatening to take over so many jobs,

asr-000521
00:51:12.300 --> 00:51:18.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: it's more important than ever because that's where we now have to make use of this different skill set.

asr-000522
00:51:18.780 --> 00:51:23.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And then my last point is early childhood education.

asr-000523
00:51:23.340 --> 00:51:25.340
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll ask more questions about it later.

asr-000524
00:51:25.420 --> 00:51:29.320
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I feel like it's an area that we can improve in.

asr-000525
00:51:29.440 --> 00:51:35.100
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'm a little bit worried about it now officially being transferred under DILG.

asr-000526
00:51:36.360 --> 00:51:38.900
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I understand the practicality of that.

asr-000527
00:51:39.040 --> 00:51:50.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I do get a little bit involved in Taguig and I see how in a city that focuses on education and will spend resources on it,

asr-000528
00:51:50.040 --> 00:51:51.000
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: then it is a good thing.

asr-000529
00:51:51.000 --> 00:51:55.380
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: But I really need to understand better how the national government,

asr-000530
00:51:55.420 --> 00:52:01.240
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: can help those LGUs that may have less resources and worse,

asr-000531
00:52:01.240 --> 00:52:11.960
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: those that may have some resources but don't choose or do not understand the importance of early childhood education.

asr-000532
00:52:11.960 --> 00:52:20.780
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So in Taguig, they have focused on, I say they because I'm not involved in the budget or the planning,

asr-000533
00:52:20.780 --> 00:52:22.820
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: on...

asr-000535
00:52:24.280 --> 00:52:30.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: hiring teachers, and this is not the case in most of the daycare centers.

asr-000536
00:52:30.280 --> 00:52:34.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: You live with what you can, whatever's there.

asr-000537
00:52:34.280 --> 00:52:36.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And they're not necessarily teachers.

asr-000538
00:52:36.280 --> 00:52:38.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And this is the formative year.

asr-000539
00:52:38.280 --> 00:52:43.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: So Secretary, I think we need to find out what your thoughts and ideas are on this.

asr-000540
00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:45.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: And I'll leave it at that.

asr-000541
00:52:45.280 --> 00:52:50.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: I'll come back after this important meeting and listen.

asr-000542
00:52:50.280 --> 00:52:52.280
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you so much, Mr. Chairman.

asr-000543
00:52:52.280 --> 00:52:53.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Salamat, Senator Pia.

asr-000544
00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:54.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Senator Erwin Tulfo.

asr-000545
00:52:54.280 --> 00:52:56.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-000546
00:52:56.380 --> 00:52:59.400
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Thank you rin, Senator Erwin at Senator Kiko.

asr-000547
00:53:00.020 --> 00:53:00.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's okay.

asr-000548
00:53:00.660 --> 00:53:02.570
Senator Pia S. Cayetano: Kasi siya lang naman yung sinisingitan ko, eh.

asr-000549
00:53:03.280 --> 00:53:04.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's alright.

asr-000550
00:53:04.280 --> 00:53:05.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's alright.

asr-000551
00:53:05.280 --> 00:53:06.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: No problem.

asr-000552
00:53:17.280 --> 00:53:23.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Good morning, Mr. Chairman, fellow senators and our officials from the Department of Education.

asr-000553
00:53:24.280 --> 00:53:29.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As we deliberate on the proposed 2027 budget of DepEd,

asr-000554
00:53:29.280 --> 00:53:34.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I would like to emphasize three priorities that deserve our urgent attention.

asr-000555
00:53:34.280 --> 00:53:38.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: More classrooms, computers, and safer schools.

asr-000556
00:53:38.280 --> 00:53:44.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Una, kailangan nating patuloy na tugunan ang kakulangan sa ating mga silid-aralan.

asr-000557
00:53:44.280 --> 00:53:48.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi po dapat patuloy na nagsisiksikan ang ating mga estudyante sa mga silid-aralan,

asr-000558
00:53:48.800 --> 00:53:53.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: o lumakad ng kilo-kilometro para makapasok lamang sa paaralan,

asr-000559
00:53:58.240 --> 00:54:04.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: o napipilitang mag-aral sa mga pasilidad na hindi naman angkop sa kanilang pangangailangan.

asr-000560
00:54:05.280 --> 00:54:13.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We must prioritize classroom construction, especially in areas where shortages are most severe,

asr-000561
00:54:13.280 --> 00:54:19.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: so that every Filipino child has access to a decent learning environment.

asr-000562
00:54:19.280 --> 00:54:21.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Second, and equally important,

asr-000563
00:54:21.280 --> 00:54:25.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: is the safety of our children inside school premises.

asr-000564
00:54:25.280 --> 00:54:31.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: The recent school shooting incidents in school grounds are a painful reminder

asr-000565
00:54:31.280 --> 00:54:36.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: that schools must be places of learning, not places of fear.

asr-000566
00:54:36.280 --> 00:54:42.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Our children should never have to worry about their safety while pursuing their education.

asr-000567
00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:50.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Na makatitiyak po ang isang magulang na makakauwi lagi ng ligtas ang kanyang anak mula sa paaralan.

asr-000568
00:54:50.280 --> 00:54:56.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ikatlo at panghuli, may mga mag-aaral po tayo, lalo na sa mga liblib na lugar,

asr-000569
00:54:56.280 --> 00:55:03.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: na hindi pa po nakakakita ng computer o hindi marunong kung pa paano gamitin ito.

asr-000570
00:55:03.280 --> 00:55:08.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As our lives intertwine with cyberspace,

asr-000571
00:55:08.280 --> 00:55:12.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: our children, particularly in the barrios,

asr-000572
00:55:12.280 --> 00:55:19.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: should be introduced to the information superhighway and to the artificial intelligence or AI.

asr-000573
00:55:19.280 --> 00:55:25.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya nais po natin malaman kung ano mga programa at pondo ang inilaan ng DepEd

asr-000574
00:55:25.280 --> 00:55:30.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: at ating bigyan ng importansya para palakasin ang school security,

asr-000575
00:55:30.280 --> 00:55:34.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: improve emergency response, provide psychosocial support,

asr-000576
00:55:34.280 --> 00:55:41.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and prevent violence within our schools and computer equipment in every classroom.

asr-000577
00:55:41.280 --> 00:55:47.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As we review this budget, let us remember that education is not simply about building classrooms and hiring teachers.

asr-000578
00:55:47.280 --> 00:55:49.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It is about

asr-000579
00:55:49.280 --> 00:55:55.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: building a future for our children and ensuring that they are safe while doing so.

asr-000580
00:55:55.280 --> 00:56:01.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because every peso we allocate must translate into better classrooms,

asr-000581
00:56:01.280 --> 00:56:06.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: better learning conditions, and safer schools for every Filipino child.

asr-000582
00:56:06.280 --> 00:56:10.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you and I look forward to a productive budget hearing. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000583
00:56:10.280 --> 00:56:13.280
