DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: This slide shows the comparison between the 2026 GAAP and General Appropriations Act

asr-001016
01:18:34.160 --> 01:18:37.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: versus the 2027 General Appropriations Bill.

asr-001017
01:18:37.940 --> 01:18:44.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Again, the rightmost side shows the decreases in parentheses in red, Mr. Chair.

asr-001018
01:18:45.020 --> 01:18:45.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001019
01:18:47.360 --> 01:18:51.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, this slide would show the General Appropriations Bill highlights,

asr-001020
01:18:52.240 --> 01:18:55.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and they're divided into four quadrants, so to speak.

asr-001021
01:18:55.480 --> 01:18:56.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, ando dun po yung personnel

asr-001022
01:18:56.440 --> 01:18:57.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: improvement.

asr-001025
01:18:57.700 --> 01:19:03.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The expanded career progression is also a reform that has been championed

asr-001026
01:19:03.780 --> 01:19:07.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: by His Honor and the Senate President and this body.

asr-001027
01:19:08.380 --> 01:19:12.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, it's getting an unprecedented level of funding at 12.09,

asr-001028
01:19:12.920 --> 01:19:16.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and we'll be able to promote 135,000 personnel.

asr-001029
01:19:17.020 --> 01:19:20.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The capacity building continues, and the RL tutors,

asr-001030
01:19:20.240 --> 01:19:23.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: this is something long awaited by our people in the field.

asr-001031
01:19:24.360 --> 01:19:26.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next is the education and system improvement,

asr-001032
01:19:26.440 --> 01:19:46.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So there's 6.4 billion for textbooks and instructional materials, plus these a loan for learning upgrade support, 9.4 billion, and then our special education programs for inclusive education including SNED, IPED, madrasa, multi-grade would total 2.78 billion.

asr-001033
01:19:46.960 --> 01:20:07.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And the third area is improving the learning environment. So for 3,800 classrooms, that would total 13.4 billion. Repairing 11,000 classrooms, 7.3 billion. ICT solutions and capacity building, 2.6 billion. That was cut. 3.1 billion was cut from that.

asr-001034
01:20:07.420 --> 01:20:13.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: One point, additional security guards for 500 billion was just an addition made by the house.

asr-001035
01:20:14.020 --> 01:20:16.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Then in the area of learner support and well-being,

asr-001036
01:20:16.960 --> 01:20:25.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Mr. Chair, nabanggit ninyong nutritious meals for kindergarten down from this year, as you mentioned, to 11.4 billion.

asr-001037
01:20:25.140 --> 01:20:45.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then yung voucher grantees naman, 2.47, 40 billion rather. I think ito din nagdagan ng 1.9 billion ng house in line with the bill you have sponsored on the K-6 expansion ng vouchers po, Your Honor.

asr-001038
01:20:45.780 --> 01:20:46.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tapos yung sa...

asr-001039
01:20:46.960 --> 01:20:59.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: bagong hire na school counselor associates and SDO counselors pursuant to the law, the mental health in basic education, which the Senate President sponsored and his honor also championed, 801 million.

asr-001040
01:21:00.140 --> 01:21:00.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001041
01:21:03.880 --> 01:21:04.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001042
01:21:05.020 --> 01:21:16.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Itong school-based feeding program natin, diyan pinapakita yung impact evaluation ng ating school feeding program, which you really helped dramatically raise.

asr-001043
01:21:16.960 --> 01:21:20.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor, this body helped raise the funding for.

asr-001044
01:21:21.000 --> 01:21:26.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, itong kita, before feeding for school year 2024-25, makikita ho sa kaliwa.

asr-001045
01:21:28.140 --> 01:21:36.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pagka nung tinimbang ho yung ating mga bata, 1.73 million ang severely wasted and wasted.

asr-001046
01:21:37.000 --> 01:21:41.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Then yung sa kanan niya, after feeding, naging 680,000 na lang.

asr-001047
01:21:41.860 --> 01:21:45.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, mahigit sa isang milyong bata ang natanggal dun sa...

asr-001048
01:21:46.960 --> 01:21:48.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: wasted or severely wasted, Your Honor.

asr-001049
01:21:49.280 --> 01:21:52.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Bukod doon, syempre yung well-documented din yung benefits

asr-001050
01:21:52.160 --> 01:21:57.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: in terms of learning gains and in terms of attendance, Your Honor.

asr-001051
01:21:57.980 --> 01:22:02.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So then in the same, the one on the right also shows the benefits

asr-001052
01:22:02.460 --> 01:22:08.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: from the feeding before and after for the next school year, Your Honor.

asr-001053
01:22:08.440 --> 01:22:16.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So yung effect po ng reform ninyo is increasing the beneficiaries

asr-001054
01:22:16.500 --> 01:22:24.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: of the feeding program by 1.2 million, 3.4 to 4.64, Your Honor.

asr-001055
01:22:25.080 --> 01:22:27.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, we'd like to acknowledge also the reforms

asr-001056
01:22:27.500 --> 01:22:31.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: under the Sagip-Saka law authored by Senator Kiko Pangilinan.

asr-001057
01:22:31.260 --> 01:22:34.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're trying to move towards increased local procurement.

asr-001058
01:22:34.180 --> 01:22:39.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And Senator Kiko has been helping us with pointing out

asr-001059
01:22:39.320 --> 01:22:42.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: who are the cooperatives in various areas that they work with

asr-001060
01:22:42.280 --> 01:22:45.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: in his capacity as chair of the Committee on Agriculture.

asr-001061
01:22:45.860 --> 01:22:46.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So nagpapasalamat.

asr-001062
01:22:46.500 --> 01:22:48.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kamatu kami doon sa tulong.

asr-001063
01:22:48.480 --> 01:22:50.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we're really trying to procure locally also,

asr-001064
01:22:51.080 --> 01:22:54.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: not only to reduce the carbon footprint,

asr-001065
01:22:54.500 --> 01:23:01.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: but also to keep our farmers and cooperatives alive and thriving, Your Honor.

asr-001066
01:23:01.980 --> 01:23:02.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001067
01:23:03.660 --> 01:23:07.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So ito pong, we were asked by the committee, Mr. Chair, Mr. President,

asr-001068
01:23:07.120 --> 01:23:11.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: to prepare some scenarios for ito pong yung various scenarios

asr-001069
01:23:11.900 --> 01:23:15.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: because we were given a GAB-level budget of 11.4 billion.

asr-001070
01:23:15.500 --> 01:23:19.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: This covers, as the chair mentioned, 25 pesos per meal

asr-001071
01:23:19.460 --> 01:23:23.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: for 3.7 million learners for 120 days.

asr-001072
01:23:23.460 --> 01:23:27.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So this includes universal kindergarten and then pursuant to our feeding law,

asr-001073
01:23:27.540 --> 01:23:30.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: severely wasted and wasted for grades 1 to 6.

asr-001074
01:23:32.100 --> 01:23:33.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And adolescent mothers pala.

asr-001075
01:23:33.520 --> 01:23:40.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: This is also a reform pushed by EDCOM to cover those who are expectant mothers.

asr-001076
01:23:40.940 --> 01:23:44.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So itong, there are four options here, Your Honor.

asr-001077
01:23:44.580 --> 01:23:45.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

asr-001078
01:23:45.500 --> 01:23:48.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: If you choose 180 days at 25 pesos per meal,

asr-001079
01:23:48.880 --> 01:23:50.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: if you go for 120 to 180,

asr-001080
01:23:50.800 --> 01:23:54.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: that will require the following amounts.

asr-001081
01:23:54.980 --> 01:24:00.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For universal kinder, 3.7, additional 9.5, and so on and so forth.

asr-001082
01:24:00.500 --> 01:24:09.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Of course, the most ambitious here would be to move to 30 pesos at 200 days,

asr-001083
01:24:09.260 --> 01:24:10.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which is the full school year.

asr-001084
01:24:11.460 --> 01:24:14.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That would require an additional 46.6 billion.

asr-001085
01:24:14.460 --> 01:24:15.340
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So that's there.

asr-001086
01:24:15.500 --> 01:24:20.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's quite a costly investment.

asr-001087
01:24:20.620 --> 01:24:27.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But I saw former Economic Planning Secretary Habito talking about it on a show the other day

asr-001088
01:24:27.420 --> 01:24:31.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: that this is one of the biggest investments we can make as a country.

asr-001089
01:24:31.580 --> 01:24:34.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Although maaring hindi natin makita kaagad yung resulta,

asr-001090
01:24:34.840 --> 01:24:39.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: definitely yun ay nagawa ng mga progressive mga bansa.

asr-001091
01:24:39.780 --> 01:24:43.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So again, thank you to this body for the support on that

asr-001092
01:24:43.360 --> 01:24:45.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and for any support that may be forthcoming.

asr-001093
01:24:45.660 --> 01:24:46.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001094
01:24:47.780 --> 01:24:51.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The Chair also mentioned school safety and security.

asr-001095
01:24:51.060 --> 01:25:01.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So nag-issue ho tayo ng panibagong DepEd Order No. 006 Guidelines on Ensuring a Safe and Motivating Learning Environment.

asr-001096
01:25:01.480 --> 01:25:05.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So bukod dun sa tighter security measures sa ating mga eskwelahan,

asr-001097
01:25:05.580 --> 01:25:11.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: more CCTV cameras, more metal detectors, improved fencing, more security guards,

asr-001098
01:25:12.380 --> 01:25:15.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: nandun din po yung mental health and safety.

asr-001099
01:25:15.500 --> 01:25:18.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Support, psychological support sa ating mga bata.

asr-001100
01:25:19.120 --> 01:25:24.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Learner support in the form of sports, scouting, school clubs.

asr-001101
01:25:26.160 --> 01:25:28.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Meron tayong national and regional telesafe hotline.

asr-001102
01:25:29.080 --> 01:25:32.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nag-hire na po tayo ng 5,400 school counselor associates.

asr-001103
01:25:32.960 --> 01:25:39.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Again, pursuant to the law passed by this body, the Mental Health in Basic Education Law.

asr-001104
01:25:39.580 --> 01:25:44.840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So kami nagpapasalamat dun dahil well-documented din ang EDCOG 2 yung kakulangan.

asr-001105
01:25:45.500 --> 01:25:47.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po yung sistema natin ng mga guidance counselors.

asr-001106
01:25:48.120 --> 01:25:52.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And this has proven to be a good workaround, institutional.

asr-001107
01:25:52.860 --> 01:25:55.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Otherwise, dead-end hood talaga tayo dito.

asr-001108
01:25:55.540 --> 01:26:00.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But now, we gave an oath to hundreds of school counselor associates yesterday.

asr-001109
01:26:01.080 --> 01:26:03.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And they're very young. They're in their 20s, fresh graduates.

asr-001110
01:26:03.920 --> 01:26:06.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And they look very excited to help our learners.

asr-001111
01:26:06.320 --> 01:26:07.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you to this body for that.

asr-001112
01:26:08.540 --> 01:26:09.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001113
01:26:10.840 --> 01:26:13.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po yung updates on incidents of school violence.

asr-001114
01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:14.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Of course, nabanggit din yung tatlong insidente.

asr-001115
01:26:15.500 --> 01:26:18.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa Tacloban, sa Sambuanga, sa South Cotabato.

asr-001116
01:26:19.440 --> 01:26:22.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, our injured learners have all been discharged.

asr-001117
01:26:23.320 --> 01:26:30.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And really, lost in the news sometimes are the heroic efforts of some of our students

asr-001118
01:26:30.180 --> 01:26:33.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: that prevented further loss of life, Your Honor.

asr-001119
01:26:33.880 --> 01:26:35.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So binigyan natin ang parangal.

asr-001120
01:26:35.280 --> 01:26:39.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Binigyan din ang Boy Scouts of the Philippines ng parangal yung two learners natin

asr-001121
01:26:39.860 --> 01:26:43.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: sa Tacloban at saka sa South Cotabato.

asr-001122
01:26:43.600 --> 01:26:50.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, again, this incident also highlighted the need for greater psychological first aid,

asr-001123
01:26:51.060 --> 01:26:53.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: mental health awareness.

asr-001124
01:26:53.380 --> 01:26:58.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, going forward, ang gusto po natin is mas marami tayong matrain

asr-001125
01:26:58.120 --> 01:27:05.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ng mga teachers natin or educators sa larangan po ng mental health and psychological first aid.

asr-001126
01:27:05.640 --> 01:27:13.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we're thankful to the DSWD, DOH for helping us, assisting us, and many in the private sector also.

asr-001127
01:27:13.600 --> 01:27:14.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, for assisting us here.

asr-001128
01:27:15.560 --> 01:27:16.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001129
01:27:17.820 --> 01:27:20.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nabanggit ni Chair yung infrastructure budget.

asr-001130
01:27:20.160 --> 01:27:21.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Again, unprecedented ho ito.

asr-001131
01:27:22.240 --> 01:27:26.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ang total infrastructure budget is 89.5 billion.

asr-001132
01:27:26.960 --> 01:27:30.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: New construction, 65.9 billion.

asr-001133
01:27:30.740 --> 01:27:32.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Repair, 7.7 billion.

asr-001134
01:27:32.880 --> 01:27:35.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And others, yung others po, yun yung nasa kanan ho.

asr-001135
01:27:36.320 --> 01:27:42.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nakalista doon school furniture, quick response, completion, mid-rise building, gabal doon.

asr-001136
01:27:42.460 --> 01:27:43.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Library hub.

asr-001137
01:27:43.600 --> 01:27:50.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Detailed engineering leasing, health facilities, inclusive learning centers, alternative learning systems, CLCs.

asr-001138
01:27:51.460 --> 01:27:53.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yun po ang breakdown nun.

asr-001139
01:27:54.540 --> 01:27:59.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And the next slide will show the implementation of such.

asr-001140
01:28:00.420 --> 01:28:03.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: As mentioned by the Chair, broken down ho ito.

asr-001141
01:28:03.460 --> 01:28:07.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, 6,000 doon sa target classrooms natin ay under DPWH.

asr-001142
01:28:07.580 --> 01:28:13.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And andi dito po si Yuse Clara to detail the program.

asr-001143
01:28:13.600 --> 01:28:14.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, ito po yung progress of this budget.

asr-001144
01:28:15.580 --> 01:28:22.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Then the LGU-led implementation is 10,671 classrooms representing 37 billion.

asr-001145
01:28:23.420 --> 01:28:31.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po ay covered by 437 MOAs or memoranda of agreement, Your Honor.

asr-001146
01:28:32.020 --> 01:28:36.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tapos meron tayong learning continuity spaces, yung dating temporary learning space.

asr-001147
01:28:36.580 --> 01:28:40.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Meron tayong last mile schools, 515 classrooms for 3 billion.

asr-001148
01:28:40.460 --> 01:28:43.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Deped acquired schools, 140 classrooms.

asr-001149
01:28:43.600 --> 01:28:46.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Totaling 18,950.

asr-001150
01:28:46.180 --> 01:28:50.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po yung total nung new construction, Your Honor.

asr-001151
01:28:50.820 --> 01:28:53.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And ang na-obligate po natin dito is around 60%.

asr-001152
01:28:53.420 --> 01:28:55.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And with a disbursement of 37.

asr-001153
01:28:57.980 --> 01:29:02.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The DPWH-led implementation, as mentioned, covers 6,000 classrooms.

asr-001154
01:29:02.760 --> 01:29:08.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We've transferred 3.75 billion as the first transfer, 2,500 classrooms.

asr-001155
01:29:08.500 --> 01:29:10.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa LGU-s po.

asr-001156
01:29:12.580 --> 01:29:13.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah.

asr-001157
01:29:13.600 --> 01:29:20.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We've covered 81 provinces, 127 cities, and 229 municipalities, Your Honor.

asr-001158
01:29:20.920 --> 01:29:23.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And they're in various stages of procurement.

asr-001159
01:29:25.680 --> 01:29:26.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001160
01:29:28.560 --> 01:29:36.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, ito po yung just detailing the coverage of the generous funding given by this body.

asr-001161
01:29:36.280 --> 01:29:43.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, 100% of provinces, 100% of cities, and 84% of municipalities are covered by the infrastructure.

asr-001162
01:29:43.600 --> 01:29:52.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, as to the budget that you have very generously provided us, Your Honor, I am told it's now 91%, sorry.

asr-001163
01:29:52.280 --> 01:29:55.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But naging kahapon 84 lang.

asr-001164
01:29:55.660 --> 01:29:56.560
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Anyway, it's now...

asr-001165
01:29:56.560 --> 01:29:57.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ninety-one percent ang?

asr-001166
01:29:57.620 --> 01:29:59.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ang coverage of municipalities, Your Honor.

asr-001167
01:29:59.120 --> 01:29:59.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Okay.

asr-001168
01:29:59.620 --> 01:30:00.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-001169
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:06.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, it's really what you have done, Your Honor, is really cover practically the whole country, Your Honor.

asr-001170
01:30:06.900 --> 01:30:13.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sorry, can I be clear lang? 91% of municipalities have a new or have classroom construction already?

asr-001171
01:30:13.780 --> 01:30:26.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Have partaken of either a new classroom or a repaired classroom or a Gabaldon building or a alternative learning center or an inclusive learning center.

asr-001172
01:30:26.200 --> 01:30:29.560
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung budget na binigay niyo po sa amin, yan po ang na-cover niya.

asr-001173
01:30:29.560 --> 01:30:34.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, it's spread all throughout the country. It's not concentrated in one place. That's what it means.

asr-001174
01:30:34.180 --> 01:30:34.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001175
01:30:35.560 --> 01:30:38.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Just to clarify, can we go a previous slide, Secretary?

asr-001176
01:30:38.840 --> 01:30:59.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, since the total here is already 65.4 billion, ibig po ba sabihin yan na meron ng MOA or nakalista na sa DPWH yung lahat ng pupondohan nating classroom based on the 2026 budget?

asr-001177
01:30:59.560 --> 01:31:01.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: May naiwan pang konti.

asr-001178
01:31:02.060 --> 01:31:03.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: May naiwan pang konti.

asr-001179
01:31:04.700 --> 01:31:07.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But the total here is already the allocation.

asr-001180
01:31:07.920 --> 01:31:09.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: About 4 billion will still be accounted for.

asr-001181
01:31:09.880 --> 01:31:16.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because ang nangyayari ngayon, minsan nagkakaroon ng aberya dun sa local government, humihingi sila ng adjustment.

asr-001182
01:31:17.140 --> 01:31:19.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we're preparing a reserve for...

asr-001183
01:31:19.500 --> 01:31:20.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's like a buffer.

asr-001184
01:31:20.380 --> 01:31:22.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Like a buffer for all of those.

asr-001185
01:31:22.220 --> 01:31:29.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But more or less, for 2026, na-identify na natin anong municipality, anong klase.

asr-001186
01:31:29.560 --> 01:31:32.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Anong facility, anong klase in classroom.

asr-001187
01:31:32.300 --> 01:31:34.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung 1, 2, 3, 1 story, 2 story.

asr-001188
01:31:35.000 --> 01:31:36.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's already identified.

asr-001189
01:31:36.420 --> 01:31:36.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001190
01:31:37.320 --> 01:31:37.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001191
01:31:37.720 --> 01:31:42.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we will end the year knowing specifically where these classrooms will be built.

asr-001192
01:31:42.520 --> 01:31:43.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001193
01:31:43.020 --> 01:31:46.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And they are in process of being procured and built.

asr-001194
01:31:46.400 --> 01:31:46.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001195
01:31:47.060 --> 01:31:47.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001196
01:31:47.280 --> 01:31:52.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And timeline-wise, and I'll ask you si Clara later, no?

asr-001197
01:31:52.120 --> 01:31:58.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But for the LGU-led and the DepEd-led, our expectation is that these classrooms will be built by...

asr-001198
01:31:59.340 --> 01:31:59.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: What?

asr-001199
01:31:59.560 --> 01:32:01.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Month next year, Secretary?

asr-001200
01:32:01.740 --> 01:32:05.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hindi natin masabi, Your Honor, because they're different types.

asr-001201
01:32:05.740 --> 01:32:07.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I think of the...

asr-001202
01:32:07.680 --> 01:32:12.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yung mga requiring demolition, you're expecting at least a 2 to 3 year horizon for those.

asr-001203
01:32:12.540 --> 01:32:14.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But yung mga simple...

asr-001204
01:32:14.620 --> 01:32:20.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Like yung learning continuity space, yun yung to respond to typhoons, et cetera.

asr-001205
01:32:20.340 --> 01:32:21.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nakatayo na yun.

asr-001206
01:32:21.360 --> 01:32:23.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Those were put up in maybe 1 to 2 months.

asr-001207
01:32:24.120 --> 01:32:28.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But the more permanent structures, you're talking maybe 1 to 2 years minimum, Your Honor.

asr-001208
01:32:28.620 --> 01:32:28.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001209
01:32:28.780 --> 01:32:35.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, hopefully, since nagsimula na naman ito, before the end of 2027, most of these will be built.

asr-001210
01:32:36.920 --> 01:32:37.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Most, yes, Your Honor.

asr-001211
01:32:37.720 --> 01:32:41.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm putting you on the spot, Secretary, para may commitment ka to everyone.

asr-001212
01:32:42.180 --> 01:32:42.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001213
01:32:42.840 --> 01:32:44.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I'm given an assurance by...

asr-001214
01:32:44.680 --> 01:32:46.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: By Yusek Cabral?

asr-001215
01:32:46.420 --> 01:32:46.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-001216
01:32:46.440 --> 01:32:49.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or which Yusek ang nag-assure po sa inyo dyan?

asr-001217
01:32:49.540 --> 01:32:50.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yusek Cabral.

asr-001218
01:32:50.300 --> 01:32:52.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But Yusek Ron is also involved.

asr-001219
01:32:52.840 --> 01:32:53.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming yung involved.

asr-001220
01:32:53.620 --> 01:32:54.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yusek as a KP.

asr-001221
01:32:54.660 --> 01:32:56.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: A lot of people working.

asr-001222
01:32:56.120 --> 01:32:57.340
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yusek Pete is also involved.

asr-001223
01:32:57.340 --> 01:32:57.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001224
01:32:57.720 --> 01:32:58.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We'll go into this in two more.

asr-001225
01:32:58.780 --> 01:32:59.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We'll go into detail during my portion.

asr-001226
01:32:59.980 --> 01:33:05.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But para lang maklaro, kasi honestly, we highlighted this in the 2026 budget.

asr-001227
01:33:06.500 --> 01:33:09.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: People are wondering nasa na ito, no?

asr-001228
01:33:09.300 --> 01:33:11.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, most of these have been...

asr-001229
01:33:11.240 --> 01:33:12.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: All of these have been identified.

asr-001230
01:33:12.900 --> 01:33:13.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that fair to say?

asr-001231
01:33:14.520 --> 01:33:15.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think 90...

asr-001232
01:33:15.820 --> 01:33:18.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I would say 97, 98% are identified.

asr-001233
01:33:19.220 --> 01:33:19.560
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Opo, opo, opo.

asr-001234
01:33:19.560 --> 01:33:28.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And therefore, it can create expectation already from our children and from their parents na pag sinabing naka-identify na, may matatayo nga.

asr-001235
01:33:28.780 --> 01:33:30.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pinoproseso yung mga mua.

asr-001236
01:33:30.660 --> 01:33:33.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero ang tanong na lang, kailan ito physically mabubuo?

asr-001237
01:33:34.040 --> 01:33:35.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct, Secretary Sani?

asr-001238
01:33:35.400 --> 01:33:36.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tama po kayo, Mr. Chair.

asr-001239
01:33:37.220 --> 01:33:40.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Now, as you know, EDCOM is building a tracker for this.

asr-001240
01:33:40.820 --> 01:33:47.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I hope DEPED can continue supporting that tracker para even yung completion ng mga classroom na ito,

asr-001241
01:33:48.180 --> 01:33:50.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: maging transparent rin sa ating mga kababayan.

asr-001242
01:33:50.340 --> 01:33:53.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because some of these will be done in 170 days, 200 days.

asr-001243
01:33:54.180 --> 01:33:56.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Some of these will take more than 300 days.

asr-001244
01:33:56.180 --> 01:33:58.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, kung malinaw na at maging malinaw,

asr-001245
01:33:58.780 --> 01:34:01.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: at least klaro sa taong bayan, klaro sa amin,

asr-001246
01:34:01.960 --> 01:34:04.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: sa napunta itong 68 billion pesos.

asr-001247
01:34:05.000 --> 01:34:07.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Now, for the benefit of everyone listening also,

asr-001248
01:34:08.080 --> 01:34:09.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the budget is good for two years, correct?

asr-001249
01:34:10.440 --> 01:34:15.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the budget that we allocated for 2026 is still live in 2027.

asr-001250
01:34:16.320 --> 01:34:18.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we would like, maybe by plenary,

asr-001251
01:34:19.260 --> 01:34:23.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: sana you could give us an assurance of what percentage of this will be completed by next year.

asr-001252
01:34:25.860 --> 01:34:28.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I'm sure, medyo huli na patapos na po.

asr-001254
01:34:28.820 --> 01:34:30.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Hindi na po ito makakompleto this year.

asr-001255
01:34:31.000 --> 01:34:32.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think that's safe to say.

asr-001256
01:34:32.560 --> 01:34:34.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, by next year, ano yung schedule of completion?

asr-001257
01:34:35.660 --> 01:34:42.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we're hoping, of course, that the majority, if not the greater majority of these classrooms will be finished by 2027.

asr-001258
01:34:42.380 --> 01:34:43.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We'll come up with an estimate, Your Honor.

asr-001259
01:34:44.060 --> 01:34:44.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. Thank you for that.

asr-001260
01:34:44.880 --> 01:34:45.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Please continue.

asr-001261
01:34:47.760 --> 01:34:48.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001262
01:34:48.920 --> 01:34:50.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001263
01:34:52.220 --> 01:34:54.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, of course, ito po yung additional portion.

asr-001264
01:34:54.800 --> 01:34:56.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ito na yung wish list portion.

asr-001265
01:34:56.040 --> 01:34:57.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Opo, opo, medyo malaki-laki po siya.

asr-001266
01:34:57.640 --> 01:34:58.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Buti lang po.

asr-001267
01:34:58.780 --> 01:35:01.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sen. Gatchalian, Pangilinan, and Tulfo are here.

asr-001268
01:35:01.520 --> 01:35:03.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sen. Hercito, to be fair,

asr-001269
01:35:03.840 --> 01:35:06.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary, kapag kami-kami nag-uusap,

asr-001270
01:35:06.720 --> 01:35:11.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ang una naming pinag-uusapan is how to bring this budget back to 4%.

asr-001271
01:35:11.340 --> 01:35:15.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's our shared goal na mabalik natin ito to 4%.

asr-001272
01:35:15.340 --> 01:35:18.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Of course, we know maraming competing interests po dito.

asr-001273
01:35:18.800 --> 01:35:21.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But we will do our best na mataas po natin ito.

asr-001274
01:35:21.700 --> 01:35:22.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Go ahead, po.

asr-001275
01:35:22.280 --> 01:35:23.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001276
01:35:23.220 --> 01:35:26.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Magandang layunin po yung 4% po talaga kasi yun talaga yung benchmark.

asr-001277
01:35:26.420 --> 01:35:27.340
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And it's a minimum.

asr-001278
01:35:27.660 --> 01:35:28.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's 4% to 6%.

asr-001279
01:35:28.700 --> 01:35:30.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's the recommendation of UNESCO, actually.

asr-001280
01:35:31.360 --> 01:35:33.340
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, medyo suntok sa buwan, ho.

asr-001281
01:35:33.500 --> 01:35:38.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But ito po nga, 147.9 billion, including our attached agencies.

asr-001282
01:35:38.520 --> 01:35:41.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, for learning recovery, the ARAL has not received any allocation.

asr-001283
01:35:41.960 --> 01:35:46.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we're asking for 15.6 billion, 1.9 billion.

asr-001284
01:35:46.320 --> 01:35:49.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 1.09 billion is the honoraria for teaching overload.

asr-001285
01:35:49.460 --> 01:35:50.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi hindi po makaka...

asr-001286
01:35:50.760 --> 01:35:52.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: If the ARAL tutor is a teacher,

asr-001287
01:35:52.860 --> 01:35:56.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they will not be entitled to the additional compensation

asr-001288
01:35:56.660 --> 01:35:58.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: unless it's an overload pay,

asr-001289
01:35:58.700 --> 01:36:04.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they have to go do it over on top of the 6R required by the Magna Carta Law for teachers, Your Honor.

asr-001290
01:36:05.280 --> 01:36:08.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, there is training for DepEd tutors of 1.75 billion.

asr-001291
01:36:08.980 --> 01:36:14.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: External tutors compensation, yung mga hindi naman DepEd teachers, 928 million.

asr-001292
01:36:15.100 --> 01:36:19.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ARAL resources, kasi nagpiprint po tayo ng resources, 4.6 billion.

asr-001293
01:36:19.900 --> 01:36:22.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Summer program, 1.2 billion.

asr-001294
01:36:23.060 --> 01:36:25.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Learning recovery and remediation consultation, 6 billion.

asr-001295
01:36:25.800 --> 01:36:28.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po yung mas malaking bagay pag pinakain po.

asr-001296
01:36:28.540 --> 01:36:32.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Mayroon natin at binigyan natin ng food allowance, yung mga teachers natin.

asr-001297
01:36:32.860 --> 01:36:36.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And just a small amount or 94 million for program management, Your Honor.

asr-001298
01:36:37.040 --> 01:36:40.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then we have the Bayang Bumabasa Initiative, led by EDCOM, 50 million.

asr-001299
01:36:41.160 --> 01:36:46.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And for personal improvement, we have 52.1 billion with the teachers, the PDOs.

asr-001300
01:36:46.880 --> 01:36:52.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And all of this is the vision of our president na talagang yung mga teachers makapag-concentrate sa pagtuturo.

asr-001301
01:36:52.420 --> 01:36:58.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kaya lahat ng school sana, mayroon tayong project development officer, mayroon tayong admin officer to sit.

asr-001302
01:36:58.540 --> 01:37:02.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung mga non-teaching-related tasks, sila na po ang gagawa.

asr-001303
01:37:03.400 --> 01:37:07.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Then we have benefits and personnel support, yung overtime pay,

asr-001304
01:37:07.600 --> 01:37:12.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: terminal leave benefits, laptops for teachers and staff, teacher training.

asr-001305
01:37:13.500 --> 01:37:17.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And for improving the learning environment, we have infrastructure for classrooms,

asr-001306
01:37:17.980 --> 01:37:21.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: classroom repairs, last-mile school buildings, pursuant to the law you passed,

asr-001307
01:37:22.440 --> 01:37:26.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 50 Gabaldon restorations, pursuant to the Gabaldon law,

asr-001308
01:37:26.440 --> 01:37:32.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: disaster preparedness, that I think we're really looking at that,

asr-001309
01:37:32.760 --> 01:37:37.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: seeing how many disasters have hit us in the past few years.

asr-001310
01:37:38.760 --> 01:37:43.840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Textbooks and instructional materials, ito po yung nirecommend ho ng EDCOM na

asr-001311
01:37:43.840 --> 01:37:52.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: bawat bata merong workbook, merong textbook, bukod sa textbook, may workbook siya na pwede niyang sulatan

asr-001312
01:37:52.000 --> 01:37:56.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: at pwede niyang iuwi at hindi na po ipapasa-pasa sana.

asr-001313
01:37:56.440 --> 01:37:58.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ibang batch.

asr-001314
01:38:00.200 --> 01:38:04.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, we're asking for additional for security guards, for metal detectors,

asr-001315
01:38:05.000 --> 01:38:09.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: for perimeter fences, Your Honor, which were not really included in the budget previously.

asr-001316
01:38:10.160 --> 01:38:10.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Next slide, please.

asr-001317
01:38:12.180 --> 01:38:15.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ito po yung second page, learner support and well-being.

asr-001318
01:38:15.240 --> 01:38:21.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa feeding, there is an additional request for 16 billion pursuant to what you mentioned,

asr-001319
01:38:21.440 --> 01:38:25.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: to have greater coverage ng Key Stage 1.

asr-001320
01:38:26.440 --> 01:38:32.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Then for the vouchers, there's an additional request for 3.5 billion.

asr-001321
01:38:32.000 --> 01:38:41.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But in fairness to the House, they granted us the 1.9 billion pursuant to the bill that you have passed, Your Honor, Mr. Chair.

asr-001322
01:38:43.180 --> 01:38:47.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So various programs, learner support programs for sports, for the Palarong Pambansa,

asr-001323
01:38:48.240 --> 01:38:53.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: for mental health and guidance counseling, totaling 13 billion.

asr-001324
01:38:53.780 --> 01:38:56.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Inclusive education, which EDCOM 2 has been forging.

asr-001327
01:38:56.240 --> 01:39:03.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Inclusive of special needs program, madrasa education, indigenous people's education, Mr. Chair.

asr-001328
01:39:03.740 --> 01:39:04.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then governance and innovation.

asr-001329
01:39:06.280 --> 01:39:15.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: This is the PQF, the Philippine Qualifications Framework, which USEC-ALDAB has been leading and really advancing,

asr-001330
01:39:16.280 --> 01:39:21.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: especially in terms of ASEAN and syncing with the world qualifications.

asr-001331
01:39:21.360 --> 01:39:22.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're playing catch-up here.

asr-001332
01:39:22.580 --> 01:39:25.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, the AI, you mentioned, it was mentioned by...

asr-001333
01:39:26.240 --> 01:39:26.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Senator Allen.

asr-001334
01:39:27.180 --> 01:39:34.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We have an e-care, the AI center, the education center for AI research, which is unfunded right now.

asr-001335
01:39:34.260 --> 01:39:37.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So we're asking for funds for that, among others.

asr-001336
01:39:37.620 --> 01:39:38.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then next slide, please.

asr-001337
01:39:39.060 --> 01:39:42.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For our attached agencies also, meron din silang mga request.

asr-001338
01:39:42.360 --> 01:39:52.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So the NBDB or the Book Development Board is requesting an additional 186.5 million for readership promotion, policy development, book fairs, research and advocacy.

asr-001339
01:39:52.980 --> 01:39:56.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, we recall the Philippines was the featured country.

asr-001340
01:39:56.360 --> 01:40:00.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The Frankfurt Book Fair, which really gave a higher profile to our publishers.

asr-001341
01:40:00.640 --> 01:40:04.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And I think really, binuhayan talaga yung book industry natin.

asr-001342
01:40:05.200 --> 01:40:12.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So I think many of our book authors, animators, book publishers are really very excited about the future prospects.

asr-001343
01:40:12.640 --> 01:40:21.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And sana ma-sustain natin ito, riding on the momentum generated by Chair Cherise during the...

asr-001344
01:40:21.100 --> 01:40:25.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, supported by our senators, Senator Loren, Frankfurt Book Fair.

asr-001345
01:40:26.220 --> 01:40:36.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The NCCT or the National Council for Children's Television, andito ko si Sir Luis, asking for 61.8 million for child-friendly, educational, and values-oriented TV content.

asr-001346
01:40:36.860 --> 01:40:43.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So ito po, siguro mahalaga ko ito, given the need to inculcate values going forward.

asr-001347
01:40:44.340 --> 01:40:55.040
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: National Museum of the Philippines, Director Barnes is here, and they're asking for an additional 255 million for digital transformation, public access, museum engagement, and component museums nationwide.

asr-001348
01:40:55.200 --> 01:40:56.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Of course, dumadamin.

asr-001349
01:40:56.220 --> 01:41:01.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Meron po yung National Museum branches natin, so they'll need additional funding for that, Mr. Chair.

asr-001350
01:41:02.040 --> 01:41:04.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Our Philippine High School for the Arts, dito po si Sir Greg.

asr-001351
01:41:05.520 --> 01:41:10.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For Campus Rehab, I visited it. It's such a beautiful structure, Mr. Chair, if you have a chance, sa Los Baños.

asr-001352
01:41:11.200 --> 01:41:25.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's a National Artist Lindy Locsin structures, but many are in disrepair, in a state of disrepair, kasi siguro they are 40, 50 years old, but really beautiful structures na huge potential na kung ma...

asr-001353
01:41:26.220 --> 01:41:38.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ma-repair po natin, and we can really inject, and of course, really produce many of our very talented artists in dance, painting, sculpture, etc., Mr. Chair.

asr-001354
01:41:38.820 --> 01:41:43.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So they're asking for 161.5 million for rehab of the campus, largely.

asr-001355
01:41:43.280 --> 01:41:55.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we have our National Academy of Sports, which is supported by many of our senators under RA 11470, asking for an additional 580 million.

asr-001356
01:41:56.220 --> 01:42:00.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So they're asking for an additional 498 million for salaries, teacher education, and many other things.

asr-001357
01:42:00.260 --> 01:42:02.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I hope you get a chance to visit sa Tarlac.

asr-001358
01:42:02.320 --> 01:42:10.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Alam po ni... nabisita na po ni Senate President yan many times, and we're thankful for the support, and hoping it can be supported going forward.

asr-001359
01:42:10.160 --> 01:42:14.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Riding on the successes of our athletes in recent competitions.

asr-001360
01:42:15.560 --> 01:42:22.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And finally, the Teacher Education Council, under... also created by the law of the Senate President, RA 11713.

asr-001361
01:42:23.180 --> 01:42:25.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So they're asking for an additional 498 million for salaries.

asr-001362
01:42:26.220 --> 01:42:30.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: education, and graduate scholarship, and regional hubs, which are mandates of the law.

asr-001363
01:42:30.720 --> 01:42:33.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor, Ili Jenny Hoxon is here with us.

asr-001364
01:42:34.820 --> 01:42:36.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yun na po ang ating presentation.

asr-001365
01:42:36.540 --> 01:42:41.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Salamat po sa ating mga mag-eating senator, Mr. President, Mr. Chair, sa inyong suporta.

asr-001366
01:42:41.760 --> 01:42:44.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At alam namin, hindi madali ang inyong trabaho.

asr-001367
01:42:44.940 --> 01:42:50.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero umaasa ho kami at humihingi ng tulong sa inyo para sa 2027.

asr-001368
01:42:51.460 --> 01:42:51.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming salamat.

asr-001369
01:42:52.080 --> 01:42:54.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Secretary Angara.

asr-001370
01:42:54.100 --> 01:42:54.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maraming salamat.

asr-001371
01:42:54.840 --> 01:42:58.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And thank you for your presentation.

asr-001372
01:42:58.880 --> 01:43:05.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, I will ask my questions, then we will have Senator Gatchalian, and then Senator Tulfo, then Senator Pangilinan.

asr-001373
01:43:07.380 --> 01:43:08.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sige, let's begin.

asr-001374
01:43:08.880 --> 01:43:12.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, maybe we can use your slides, Secretary Angara.

asr-001375
01:43:12.420 --> 01:43:14.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Could we go to the...

asr-001376
01:43:14.180 --> 01:43:19.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, my first three areas are on the classroom, school safety, and the feeding program.

asr-001377
01:43:19.960 --> 01:43:23.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But you've clarified many things, so ano lang po ito, follow-up na lang ito, no?

asr-001378
01:43:23.840 --> 01:43:24.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, the board...

asr-001379
01:43:24.840 --> 01:43:28.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Booth, can we go to the slides on...

asr-001380
01:43:28.040 --> 01:43:29.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maybe we can start with the classrooms.

asr-001381
01:43:31.540 --> 01:43:33.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, unang-una, Secretary.

asr-001382
01:43:33.340 --> 01:43:39.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In the video, may naka-identify na 23,000 classrooms completed.

asr-001383
01:43:41.440 --> 01:43:44.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: When were these done?

asr-001384
01:43:45.200 --> 01:43:50.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or does this include the target of 18,950 from this year?

asr-001385
01:43:50.580 --> 01:43:50.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001386
01:43:54.840 --> 01:44:06.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: These are those which were completed as of October of this year, and began as early as 2022, Your Honor.

asr-001387
01:44:06.700 --> 01:44:08.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung cut-off niya is when it was completed.

asr-001388
01:44:09.080 --> 01:44:11.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung funding year niya is several years.

asr-001389
01:44:11.180 --> 01:44:14.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Could be 2022, could be 2023, could be 2024.

asr-001390
01:44:14.760 --> 01:44:21.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, 23,000 classrooms were built from 2022 to 2025?

asr-001391
01:44:22.240 --> 01:44:22.840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's correct.

asr-001392
01:44:23.480 --> 01:44:23.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Completed.

asr-001393
01:44:23.960 --> 01:44:24.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Completed.

asr-001397
01:44:24.840 --> 01:44:27.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, maaaring nag-start previously, Your Honor.

asr-001398
01:44:27.540 --> 01:44:31.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maaaring napondohan earlier than 2022?

asr-001399
01:44:31.420 --> 01:44:32.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maaaring, ho.

asr-001400
01:44:32.140 --> 01:44:32.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maaaring.

asr-001401
01:44:32.560 --> 01:44:32.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001402
01:44:33.020 --> 01:44:35.220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, okay.

asr-001403
01:44:35.440 --> 01:44:41.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Because if you remember last year, remember in that hearing, Yusec Lara was there.

asr-001404
01:44:41.820 --> 01:44:47.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We knew that the completed classrooms of 2025 was less than 200, right?

asr-001405
01:44:47.380 --> 01:44:47.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-001406
01:44:48.100 --> 01:44:48.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Diba?

asr-001407
01:44:48.520 --> 01:44:49.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: For 2025.

asr-001408
01:44:50.560 --> 01:44:54.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, these were done in 2022.

asr-001409
01:44:54.720 --> 01:44:54.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 2022.

asr-001410
01:44:54.800 --> 01:44:55.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 2022?

asr-001411
01:44:55.120 --> 01:44:55.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-001412
01:44:55.640 --> 01:44:59.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think there's a long, really a long, I don't know what you call it, gestation or

asr-001421
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:09.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Construction period ho. Kasi from validation to bidding to completion, it's really 2 to 3 years for one classroom.

asr-001422
01:45:09.680 --> 01:45:15.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. So, potentially, these were classrooms funded in 2020, 2019, 2018, no?

asr-001423
01:45:15.880 --> 01:45:20.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, not really. I recall during the pandemic, wala ho tayong masyadong funding.

asr-001424
01:45:20.000 --> 01:45:24.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, 2020, 2021, very minimal ang funding ho natin for classrooms.

asr-001425
01:45:24.440 --> 01:45:28.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But maaaring could be even previous kasi natenga during the pandemic ho.

asr-001426
01:45:28.280 --> 01:45:30.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, nag-continue na lang ho afterwards.

asr-001427
01:45:30.840 --> 01:45:34.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because we were, we had the longest lockdown.

asr-001428
01:45:34.360 --> 01:45:39.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we were out of school. We were doing study from home for over 2 years.

asr-001429
01:45:39.020 --> 01:45:40.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we didn't really build during that time, no?

asr-001430
01:45:40.640 --> 01:45:44.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Wala po. Kasi nire-direct ho sa ayuda ho yung classroom funds that time.

asr-001431
01:45:44.680 --> 01:45:50.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yusek Ron is here. Are these still the PPP schools? Or would you know, Yusek Ron?

asr-001432
01:45:50.260 --> 01:45:52.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: No, I think the PPP schools, Your Honor, natapos na yung 2022.

asr-001433
01:45:53.440 --> 01:45:57.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think, but a lot of, maybe some. May konti na lang ho.

asr-001434
01:45:58.200 --> 01:45:58.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Okay.

asr-001435
01:45:58.280 --> 01:46:02.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero yung last payments for the Aquino PPPs were 2022.

asr-001436
01:46:02.580 --> 01:46:06.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. So, definitely not the PPP during the Aquino administration.

asr-001437
01:46:07.100 --> 01:46:10.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There was some classroom construction done during the Duterte administration.

asr-001438
01:46:11.060 --> 01:46:13.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is possibly, possibly that, right?

asr-001439
01:46:13.780 --> 01:46:15.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yung iba ho. Mga maaaring na umpisa.

asr-001440
01:46:15.860 --> 01:46:18.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero na-complete na lang ho. It's really hard to track the,

asr-001441
01:46:18.880 --> 01:46:23.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: because there's a different construction timeline for every area ho.

asr-001442
01:46:23.860 --> 01:46:28.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. I'm only asking because we've always started with 165,000 classrooms.

asr-001443
01:46:28.280 --> 01:46:29.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's always been our number.

asr-001444
01:46:30.740 --> 01:46:39.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But with the 23,000 completion, does that mean that we're lower by, we're now at 140,000?

asr-001445
01:46:39.480 --> 01:46:41.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Around. Thereabouts. 142,000.

asr-001446
01:46:41.360 --> 01:46:43.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Para we can also update our figures, no?

asr-001447
01:46:43.960 --> 01:46:44.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001448
01:46:44.940 --> 01:46:48.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: O, sige. So, anyway, si Carol naman is here. I'm sure he's behind me, no?

asr-001449
01:46:48.660 --> 01:46:50.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Napifil ko yung presence. Nandiyan ba siya?

asr-001450
01:46:50.380 --> 01:46:51.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Napifil ko yung presence niya.

asr-001451
01:46:52.500 --> 01:46:57.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maybe by the plenary secretary, we can drill down para even in our statements,

asr-001452
01:46:57.420 --> 01:46:58.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: in our,

asr-001453
01:46:58.200 --> 01:46:59.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: in our speeches,

asr-001454
01:46:59.900 --> 01:47:03.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we can clarify what the gap is at this point, no?

asr-001455
01:47:04.480 --> 01:47:07.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, Yusek C., would you want to add anything to the discussion?

asr-001456
01:47:07.480 --> 01:47:10.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: He's mentioning some classrooms even took five years, Your Honor.

asr-001457
01:47:10.260 --> 01:47:13.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Baka dati kasi nga pandemic, natenga yun ng pandemic.

asr-001458
01:47:13.320 --> 01:47:17.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Basta huwag nating ulitin yun, Secretary, na five years to yung pondong ito.

asr-001459
01:47:17.180 --> 01:47:19.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Dapat one year, gawa na talaga siya.

asr-001460
01:47:19.340 --> 01:47:21.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. So, let me go back to the classrooms.

asr-001461
01:47:23.100 --> 01:47:25.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May we see by the plenary,

asr-001462
01:47:25.900 --> 01:47:27.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the list,

asr-001463
01:47:27.540 --> 01:47:35.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the plan for the 65 billion pesos from the DPWH and from the LGU-led and DEPED-led.

asr-001464
01:47:36.620 --> 01:47:40.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We would like to see by the plenary, the list of the classrooms.

asr-001465
01:47:40.920 --> 01:47:41.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-001466
01:47:41.480 --> 01:47:43.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we can also publish it, no?

asr-001467
01:47:43.500 --> 01:47:49.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And at least the, not just the mayors, but even the parents and the children,

asr-001468
01:47:50.200 --> 01:47:53.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: alam nila, meron ang expectation of where these classrooms will be built.

asr-001469
01:47:54.220 --> 01:47:57.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yusek Lara, could you give us an update on the DPWH-led classrooms?

asr-001470
01:47:57.540 --> 01:48:02.320
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: Good morning, Mr. Chair. Good morning, Secretary, and the Honorable Senators.

asr-001471
01:48:02.780 --> 01:48:07.500
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: For the 6,000 classrooms for DPWH in the 2026 fund,

asr-001472
01:48:08.040 --> 01:48:11.860
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: we've advertised 7 billion, around 2,000 classrooms.

asr-001473
01:48:12.540 --> 01:48:16.860
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: And then we're at post-qualification, finishing post-qualification,

asr-001474
01:48:17.160 --> 01:48:22.420
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: and short of award or awarded for 1.87 billion, which is 533 classrooms.

asr-001475
01:48:23.080 --> 01:48:26.200
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: I'll just say here already,

asr-001479
01:48:27.420 --> 01:48:29.560
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We've been encountering quite a few failure of biddings.

asr-001480
01:48:29.680 --> 01:48:35.120
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: They've been concerned with the costing of classrooms with fuel price increases.

asr-001481
01:48:35.440 --> 01:48:41.140
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: So, they were a bit market-sounding, gave us some feedback that it was quite low,

asr-001482
01:48:41.220 --> 01:48:45.160
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: but we're repackaging it to be more attractive to prospective bidders.

asr-001483
01:48:45.260 --> 01:48:53.900
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We always just repackage it in order to minimize, extend spending on mobilization.

asr-001484
01:48:53.900 --> 01:48:57.020
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: So, we cluster it in a better location.

asr-001485
01:48:57.020 --> 01:48:58.180
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: More strategic locations.

asr-001486
01:48:58.360 --> 01:49:03.020
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: But yes, we've been encountering, Senator, quite a few failure of biddings.

asr-001487
01:49:03.040 --> 01:49:07.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is it correct, the MOA that you signed was worth about 20 billion pesos, right?

asr-001488
01:49:07.200 --> 01:49:07.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Tama, di ba?

asr-001489
01:49:07.680 --> 01:49:07.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-001490
01:49:08.100 --> 01:49:08.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Around 20 billion.

asr-001491
01:49:09.080 --> 01:49:09.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 6,000 classrooms.

asr-001492
01:49:10.040 --> 01:49:10.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, so...

asr-001493
01:49:10.820 --> 01:49:11.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 1.4 billion, yes, Your Honor.

asr-001494
01:49:11.700 --> 01:49:11.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sorry?

asr-001495
01:49:12.080 --> 01:49:12.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 21.4 billion.

asr-001496
01:49:12.880 --> 01:49:13.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 21.4.

asr-001497
01:49:13.720 --> 01:49:15.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, of the 21.4, Yusec Lara,

asr-001498
01:49:17.780 --> 01:49:21.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ilan doon yung meron ng bidder at meron ng gagawa?

asr-001499
01:49:21.360 --> 01:49:24.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At ilan doon yung di pa kayo nakakapaghanap ng bidder at gagawa?

asr-001500
01:49:24.720 --> 01:49:26.620
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: 1.87 billion.

asr-001501
01:49:26.620 --> 01:49:31.780
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We have bidders, prospective bidders, well, already submitted bids.

asr-001502
01:49:32.560 --> 01:49:35.260
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: And some are already NTP or short of award.

asr-001503
01:49:35.420 --> 01:49:39.240
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: And then 7B, 2,000 classrooms were advertised.

asr-001504
01:49:41.000 --> 01:49:47.760
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We've had attendees in our pre-bid conference, but still no assurance on if they will submit.

asr-001505
01:49:47.960 --> 01:49:49.020
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: But these are ongoing.

asr-001506
01:49:49.440 --> 01:49:52.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, but that's 1.8, is that correct?

asr-001507
01:49:52.720 --> 01:49:53.300
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: 1.8.

asr-001508
01:49:53.360 --> 01:49:55.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 1.8 out of 21.4.

asr-001509
01:49:55.260 --> 01:49:56.260
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: Yes, only that...

asr-001510
01:49:56.620 --> 01:49:58.900
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: Amount is successful in our...

asr-001511
01:49:58.900 --> 01:49:59.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001512
01:50:04.120 --> 01:50:05.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's very low.

asr-001513
01:50:05.400 --> 01:50:06.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's a low...

asr-001514
01:50:06.160 --> 01:50:09.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's a very low amount, ang baba niyan, no?

asr-001515
01:50:09.860 --> 01:50:15.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, kasi my understanding with the LGU-led is the MOA's are already there.

asr-001516
01:50:16.040 --> 01:50:17.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, pinaproseso na po yan.

asr-001517
01:50:17.740 --> 01:50:19.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct, Secretary Sani?

asr-001518
01:50:19.460 --> 01:50:25.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, yung natirang 40 plus billion na yan, meron ng identified yan ng mga LGUs?

asr-001519
01:50:25.360 --> 01:50:26.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001520
01:50:26.040 --> 01:50:26.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct po, no?

asr-001521
01:50:26.620 --> 01:50:27.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tama naman, no?

asr-001522
01:50:27.280 --> 01:50:27.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tama po.

asr-001523
01:50:28.900 --> 01:50:31.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And some of them, these are in different stages.

asr-001524
01:50:31.340 --> 01:50:36.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May mga ilan, advanced na, meaning nag-groundbreaking na, kasi may nag-groundbreaking na yun akong napuntahan.

asr-001525
01:50:37.080 --> 01:50:42.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May mga iba, nagba-back and forth pa dun sa final designs, no?

asr-001526
01:50:42.940 --> 01:50:43.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001527
01:50:43.580 --> 01:50:44.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct?

asr-001528
01:50:44.720 --> 01:50:46.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, that's correct, Your Honor.

asr-001529
01:50:46.160 --> 01:50:47.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In fact, there's some under construction already.

asr-001530
01:50:47.860 --> 01:50:50.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I've seen it in Region 8.

asr-001531
01:50:50.260 --> 01:50:50.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001532
01:50:50.740 --> 01:50:56.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Has there been any feedback with regard to failing bid?

asr-001533
01:50:56.620 --> 01:51:00.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or difficulty in completion of the schools?

asr-001534
01:51:01.640 --> 01:51:02.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi ako, wala akong naririnig.

asr-001535
01:51:02.920 --> 01:51:07.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Wala pa, pero kasi ina-anticipate nung ibang LGU and they ask for a cost adjustment, Your Honor.

asr-001536
01:51:07.900 --> 01:51:08.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Okay.

asr-001537
01:51:08.440 --> 01:51:15.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we have a 10% ban na pagpasok dun, ginagrant na namin automatically because we acknowledge that, as mentioned by you, si Clara,

asr-001538
01:51:15.980 --> 01:51:18.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: meron na iba na talaga yung presyo ng mga kagamitan.

asr-001539
01:51:18.380 --> 01:51:22.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, in fact, in the last hearing that we had, I was surprised that your price was still that low

asr-001540
01:51:22.820 --> 01:51:25.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: considering nag-Iran war na, nagtaas na yung presyo ng mga bansang.

asr-001541
01:51:26.620 --> 01:51:27.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Bagay-bagay.

asr-001542
01:51:27.320 --> 01:51:29.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, you've adjusted, but there are still no takers.

asr-001543
01:51:30.000 --> 01:51:30.820
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We've adjusted.

asr-001544
01:51:31.280 --> 01:51:38.460
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: Actually, Senator, the 7 billion, we have prospective bidders, but still around 2 to 3 weeks of remaining procurement time.

asr-001545
01:51:38.460 --> 01:51:48.540
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: So, 7B, some of these were already advertised again or advertised a second time, and we've already come up with prospective bidders.

asr-001546
01:51:48.680 --> 01:51:48.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001547
01:51:50.140 --> 01:51:54.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If by the, and I don't know, is there a DBM representative here?

asr-001548
01:51:56.100 --> 01:51:56.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-001549
01:51:56.620 --> 01:51:57.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, ayan si ma'am pala.

asr-001550
01:51:57.820 --> 01:51:58.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ms. Labastilla.

asr-001551
01:51:59.800 --> 01:52:05.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nag-moa na ho sila, pero kung hindi ito ma-fulfill, pwede pa bang ibalik yan sa DepEd?

asr-001552
01:52:06.420 --> 01:52:07.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pwede pa ba po?

asr-001553
01:52:07.200 --> 01:52:08.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pwede po ba yun?

asr-001554
01:52:08.640 --> 01:52:11.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kunyari, hindi nila matapos by the end of the year, you si Clara.

asr-001555
01:52:12.120 --> 01:52:16.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Anyway, ikaw naman nagsabi, 1.7 out of 21.4 lang palang nabibid nila.

asr-001556
01:52:17.020 --> 01:52:18.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pwede pa bang ibalik yun sa DepEd?

asr-001557
01:52:19.060 --> 01:52:20.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pandagdag dun sa LGU-LED?

asr-001558
01:52:21.140 --> 01:52:21.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that possible?

asr-001559
01:52:22.820 --> 01:52:24.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi alam ko na transfer na to, di ba?

asr-001560
01:52:24.740 --> 01:52:25.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Malipat na siya.

asr-001561
01:52:25.640 --> 01:52:26.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct, no?

asr-001562
01:52:26.620 --> 01:52:28.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, no, it's with DBM pa rin?

asr-001563
01:52:29.300 --> 01:52:32.740
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: The funds transferred is only 7 billion.

asr-001564
01:52:33.140 --> 01:52:34.760
DPWH OIC Undersecretary Lara Marisse I. Esquibil: We haven't transferred 13 billion.

asr-001565
01:52:34.760 --> 01:52:42.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, can I ask Director Vivian, pwede pa po ba yung, kasi remember we had a hearing,

asr-001566
01:52:42.380 --> 01:52:48.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ang sabi natin at the end of the year, chicheck natin anong kabayo yung pinaka mabilis at efficient.

asr-001567
01:52:48.600 --> 01:52:49.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: PPP ba ito?

asr-001568
01:52:50.380 --> 01:52:51.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: DPWH led ba ito?

asr-001569
01:52:51.680 --> 01:52:53.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or DepEd and LGU led ba ito?

asr-001570
01:52:53.900 --> 01:52:54.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Di ba?

asr-001571
01:52:54.600 --> 01:52:55.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we're already there.

asr-001572
01:52:55.540 --> 01:52:56.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nandito na tayo sa end of the year.

asr-001573
01:52:56.600 --> 01:52:58.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nakikita natin anong gumagalaw, anong di gumagalaw.

asr-001574
01:52:59.920 --> 01:53:05.100
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is it still possible to allocate it in a different way, Director Vivian?

asr-001575
01:53:05.880 --> 01:53:07.560
DBM Budget and Management Bureau-F Director Vivien V. Labastilla: Magandang umaga po, Mr. Chair.

asr-001576
01:53:07.720 --> 01:53:11.220
DBM Budget and Management Bureau-F Director Vivien V. Labastilla: Yes po, since hindi pa naman natatransfer din yung cash.

asr-001577
01:53:11.540 --> 01:53:11.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sige.

asr-001578
01:53:12.200 --> 01:53:14.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Our plenary is end of November.

asr-001579
01:53:14.540 --> 01:53:17.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If I'm not mistaken, November 24 or 25.

asr-001580
01:53:19.120 --> 01:53:20.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: End of the year na yun.

asr-001581
01:53:20.460 --> 01:53:21.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Di ba, end of the year na yun.

asr-001582
01:53:21.600 --> 01:53:22.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Baka maganda yun si Clara.

asr-001583
01:53:22.780 --> 01:53:24.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung wala pa rin talagang bidder,

asr-001584
01:53:24.800 --> 01:53:33.820
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: can we please consider that Seksani with Sek Vins and with Secretary Kim of DBM,

asr-001585
01:53:34.500 --> 01:53:39.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: can we still talk, can we consider that if that's another month from now, Yusek Lara?

asr-001586
01:53:40.340 --> 01:53:43.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi kung di talaga yan gumagalaw, doon na tayo kung saan gagalaw.

asr-001587
01:53:43.800 --> 01:53:46.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will accede to what the committee wants.

asr-001588
01:53:46.580 --> 01:53:48.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: No, it's actually an executive already.

asr-001589
01:53:48.840 --> 01:53:51.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's not our call anymore, SP, di ba?

asr-001590
01:53:51.540 --> 01:53:54.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Hindi natin call ito kasi na-allocate na po natin ito.

asr-001591
01:53:54.800 --> 01:53:57.220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's really an executive decision at this point.

asr-001592
01:53:57.380 --> 01:54:02.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But I hope we can have another update by the plenary, Secretary Sani.

asr-001593
01:54:02.460 --> 01:54:05.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We'll probably ask Secretary Vins also during the plenary for DPWH.

asr-001594
01:54:06.700 --> 01:54:08.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pero considering October na,

asr-001595
01:54:11.420 --> 01:54:13.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: my simple math is 5%.

asr-001596
01:54:13.620 --> 01:54:16.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Parang 5% pa lang yung napapabid out ninyo.

asr-001597
01:54:17.800 --> 01:54:20.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 8%? Okay, 8% pa lang napapabid out ninyo.

asr-001598
01:54:20.360 --> 01:54:21.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 92% pa yan.

asr-001599
01:54:22.380 --> 01:54:24.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Doon natin siya ilagay sa kabayong.

asr-001600
01:54:24.800 --> 01:54:27.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Huwag na dun sa kabayong hindi gumagalaw, di ba?

asr-001601
01:54:27.380 --> 01:54:28.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's my take, no?

asr-001602
01:54:28.460 --> 01:54:29.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And I hope you can discuss that.

asr-001603
01:54:30.160 --> 01:54:33.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Just a qualification on what we've said, Mr. Chair, with your permission.

asr-001604
01:54:33.960 --> 01:54:37.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I was told by our Yusek for Finance that yung transfer na 7B,

asr-001605
01:54:37.840 --> 01:54:40.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi na po pwedeng ibalik sa amin yung funds na yun.

asr-001606
01:54:40.600 --> 01:54:41.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Okay, so we're talking about the balance.

asr-001607
01:54:41.720 --> 01:54:42.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yung 13 na lang siguro.

asr-001608
01:54:42.840 --> 01:54:45.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero yung 7, kasi nasa treasury na ho daw yun.

asr-001609
01:54:46.020 --> 01:54:51.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 13 billion, ilang libo yun?

asr-001610
01:54:51.020 --> 01:54:52.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ilang libo yung classroom pa yun?

asr-001611
01:54:53.300 --> 01:54:54.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Napakarami pa siguro nun, no?

asr-001612
01:54:54.800 --> 01:54:56.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Several thousand.

asr-001613
01:54:56.800 --> 01:54:57.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Several thousand.

asr-001614
01:54:57.560 --> 01:54:58.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Mga 4,000.

asr-001615
01:54:58.320 --> 01:54:59.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's 4,000.

asr-001616
01:54:59.720 --> 01:54:59.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yeah.

asr-001617
01:55:00.340 --> 01:55:01.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So please consider that.

asr-001618
01:55:01.240 --> 01:55:05.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung hindi talaga kaya, doon tayo sa gumagalaw, no?

asr-001619
01:55:06.240 --> 01:55:06.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay?

asr-001620
01:55:06.880 --> 01:55:08.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Please consider that.

asr-001621
01:55:09.880 --> 01:55:15.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary Sani, so 8950, so the commitment of DPWH,

asr-001622
01:55:15.940 --> 01:55:20.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the commitment of DPWH is 13,950 classrooms.

asr-001623
01:55:21.560 --> 01:55:22.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct, no?

asr-001624
01:55:22.060 --> 01:55:23.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi 8950 ito.

asr-001625
01:55:23.920 --> 01:55:24.780
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We'll leave.

asr-001626
01:55:24.800 --> 01:55:29.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We'll leave the 6,000 to DPWH, so 3950 is the commitment.

asr-001627
01:55:29.620 --> 01:55:33.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ang tanong na lang kung magagawa ba ito by 2027 or 2028?

asr-001628
01:55:33.320 --> 01:55:33.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-001629
01:55:34.020 --> 01:55:38.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, and correct to say that 97% of this, nasimulan na?

asr-001630
01:55:40.720 --> 01:55:42.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In various stages, Your Honor.

asr-001631
01:55:42.160 --> 01:55:42.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-001632
01:55:42.540 --> 01:55:42.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nasimulan?

asr-001633
01:55:43.140 --> 01:55:43.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Basta nasimulan?

asr-001634
01:55:43.820 --> 01:55:44.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Na-identify?

asr-001635
01:55:44.720 --> 01:55:45.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, yes, Your Honor.

asr-001636
01:55:45.500 --> 01:55:47.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, so we've identified them.

asr-001637
01:55:47.100 --> 01:55:49.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We're in the process of finalizing the MOAs.

asr-001638
01:55:49.920 --> 01:55:51.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung iba nag-groundbreaking na.

asr-001639
01:55:51.160 --> 01:55:55.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung iba nag-go back and forth pa.

asr-001640
01:55:55.640 --> 01:55:55.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Apo.

asr-001641
01:55:56.280 --> 01:55:56.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct, no?

asr-001642
01:55:56.880 --> 01:55:57.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Correct, ko.

asr-001643
01:55:57.440 --> 01:55:57.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, sige.

asr-001644
01:55:58.020 --> 01:56:02.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So can we please, because by the way, pagdating ng plenary, I'm the one defending you.

asr-001645
01:56:02.180 --> 01:56:02.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001646
01:56:02.660 --> 01:56:04.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So tatanungin rin ako nito eh, di ba?

asr-001647
01:56:04.380 --> 01:56:08.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So I hope we can have an update by November.

asr-001648
01:56:08.600 --> 01:56:08.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Of course.

asr-001649
01:56:09.120 --> 01:56:10.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think we're November 24, ba?

asr-001650
01:56:11.720 --> 01:56:14.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: November 24, ang plenary ng DepEd.

asr-001651
01:56:14.380 --> 01:56:20.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And to also support your chairman to defend this, please help us.

asr-001652
01:56:20.580 --> 01:56:21.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Please continue.

asr-001653
01:56:21.560 --> 01:56:25.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I know that in the last few months, you've been really fast-tracking all of the MOAs, no?

asr-001654
01:56:25.720 --> 01:56:30.640
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sana tuloy-tuloy po ito para pagdating ng November 24, kapag kaharap na natin yung buong Senado,

asr-001655
01:56:31.120 --> 01:56:32.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we can really defend this budget, no?

asr-001656
01:56:32.780 --> 01:56:33.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-001657
01:56:33.460 --> 01:56:33.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will do that.

asr-001658
01:56:34.400 --> 01:56:39.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So for 2027, we have 30 billion allocated for the classrooms, no?

asr-001659
01:56:40.900 --> 01:56:46.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And I take it that this will move faster than 2026.

asr-001660
01:56:46.260 --> 01:56:47.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that correct, Secretary Sani?

asr-001661
01:56:47.580 --> 01:56:50.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, I think we still have time to do.

asr-001662
01:56:50.580 --> 01:56:51.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Early procurement.

asr-001663
01:56:51.340 --> 01:56:55.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So if we have certainty as to the number, if we know it's not going to go down anymore,

asr-001664
01:56:55.620 --> 01:56:57.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: we can commence early procurement.

asr-001665
01:56:57.380 --> 01:57:02.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But we did that in 2025, Your Honor, and the number changed at the BICAM.

asr-001666
01:57:02.320 --> 01:57:05.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So nasira ho yung early procurement activities namin.

asr-001667
01:57:06.140 --> 01:57:10.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because hinati yung inalat for classrooms.

asr-001668
01:57:10.740 --> 01:57:14.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So the early procurement was for not, but that would have saved several months.

asr-001669
01:57:15.300 --> 01:57:17.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And that was construction time.

asr-001670
01:57:17.600 --> 01:57:19.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So by January, ma-award na sana yun.

asr-001671
01:57:19.400 --> 01:57:20.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, okay.

asr-001672
01:57:20.580 --> 01:57:24.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung list of classrooms natin, I'm assuming naka-priority ito, di ba, by area.

asr-001673
01:57:25.120 --> 01:57:28.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So may mga hindi tayo na hahagit, di ba?

asr-001674
01:57:28.800 --> 01:57:32.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So meaning, kunyari, kung ang priority ng isang lugar, 50 classrooms,

asr-001675
01:57:32.920 --> 01:57:35.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but they probably submit a list of 70 classrooms or even more.

asr-001676
01:57:35.720 --> 01:57:36.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Meron hung gano'n.

asr-001677
01:57:36.540 --> 01:57:36.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Di ba?

asr-001678
01:57:37.040 --> 01:57:40.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So meaning, yung identification nitong next batch should be easier already

asr-001679
01:57:40.840 --> 01:57:42.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: because we already have all the data.

asr-001680
01:57:42.760 --> 01:57:43.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, and we have the validation.

asr-001681
01:57:44.700 --> 01:57:47.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The validation is in a more advanced stage also, Your Honor.

asr-001682
01:57:47.380 --> 01:57:47.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-001683
01:57:48.020 --> 01:57:49.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We don't revalidate every year naman, di ba?

asr-001684
01:57:49.900 --> 01:57:52.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: The validation that we did for this year is good for next year.

asr-001685
01:57:52.300 --> 01:57:53.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It should be, Your Honor.

asr-001686
01:57:53.280 --> 01:57:53.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It should be, right?

asr-001687
01:57:54.560 --> 01:57:59.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So the identification of these 30 billion should be faster also.

asr-001688
01:57:59.700 --> 01:58:00.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001689
01:58:00.480 --> 01:58:00.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-001690
01:58:01.600 --> 01:58:07.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: There's a suggestion among the senators which we can take offline also.

asr-001691
01:58:07.660 --> 01:58:12.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If we need to identify, considering we already have all the data

asr-001692
01:58:12.660 --> 01:58:16.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and all the submissions and as being former chairman of finance,

asr-001693
01:58:16.400 --> 01:58:18.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: you know that we also have all these folders, no?

asr-001694
01:58:18.900 --> 01:58:19.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Senator JV, may isang...

asr-001695
01:58:19.900 --> 01:58:21.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Opsiya na yan, worth of folders at this point.

asr-001696
01:58:23.580 --> 01:58:26.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Would it be better, and maybe I can ask DBM also,

asr-001697
01:58:27.020 --> 01:58:31.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: would it be better to identify the areas

asr-001698
01:58:31.160 --> 01:58:36.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or would you suggest we still give it to DepEd to have that leeway?

asr-001699
01:58:37.200 --> 01:58:41.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I understand kasi this year, ang laki ng allocation and it was a big jump,

asr-001700
01:58:42.120 --> 01:58:46.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: so it was almost impossible to identify it by December of 2025.

asr-001701
01:58:46.000 --> 01:58:49.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But for 2027, the data is there already.

asr-001702
01:58:49.900 --> 01:58:51.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We can already identify.

asr-001703
01:58:52.460 --> 01:58:55.580
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Would it make sense to identify the 30 billion?

asr-001704
01:58:55.800 --> 01:58:56.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I-specific na siya?

asr-001705
01:58:56.840 --> 01:58:59.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or would you suggest to just keep it broad?

asr-001706
01:58:59.840 --> 01:59:03.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maybe not down to the school level, Your Honor, because in the past, that was done.

asr-001707
01:59:03.380 --> 01:59:08.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But because of issues on the ground, whether legal questions or ownership issues,

asr-001708
01:59:09.080 --> 01:59:10.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: may mga schools na hindi natuloy.

asr-001709
01:59:10.860 --> 01:59:15.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So then that money could no longer be transferred or used for other projects.

asr-001710
01:59:15.280 --> 01:59:16.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So just to...

asr-001711
01:59:16.860 --> 01:59:19.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That would make our life easier than we just follow.

asr-001712
01:59:19.380 --> 01:59:19.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But of course...

asr-001713
01:59:20.060 --> 01:59:22.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: There is a cost to that and that is the inflexibility, Your Honor.

asr-001714
01:59:22.620 --> 01:59:25.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yeah, so you're suggesting we just continue the process?

asr-001715
01:59:25.420 --> 01:59:31.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Or provide what area should be prioritized, last mile schools or those with double and triple shifts, as you mentioned.

asr-001716
01:59:32.180 --> 01:59:36.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Those with the highest congestion.

asr-001717
01:59:36.500 --> 01:59:38.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So we can include that in the...

asr-001718
01:59:38.260 --> 01:59:42.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maybe a general qualification that allows for a certain degree of flexibility, Your Honor, would make sense.

asr-001719
01:59:43.740 --> 01:59:45.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Director Vivian, do you agree?

asr-001720
01:59:46.760 --> 01:59:49.500
DBM Budget and Management Bureau-F Director Vivien V. Labastilla: Mr. Chair, yes, we respectfully agree.

asr-001721
01:59:49.900 --> 01:59:51.540
DBM Budget and Management Bureau-F Director Vivien V. Labastilla: With Secretary Angara.

asr-001722
01:59:51.720 --> 01:59:52.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, thank you.

asr-001723
01:59:52.760 --> 01:59:53.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, sige.

asr-001724
01:59:53.400 --> 01:59:54.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Let's leave the classrooms for now.

asr-001725
01:59:54.980 --> 01:59:56.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Let's go to the feeding program.

asr-001726
01:59:56.900 --> 01:59:57.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So ito naman...

asr-001727
01:59:57.460 --> 01:59:58.460
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Um...

asr-001728
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:05.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: This is a LEDOC, as Secretary Sani knows and the Senate President knows, this is a LEDOC measure.

asr-001729
02:00:07.220 --> 02:00:17.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And the feeding program is probably one of our biggest contributions to decrease our learning gap.

asr-001730
02:00:17.960 --> 02:00:21.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung mapondohan po natin ito at ma-implement natin na maayos,

asr-001731
02:00:23.520 --> 02:00:27.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: many of our issues in our schools should be solved.

asr-001732
02:00:27.380 --> 02:00:33.620
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or this will help in a big way yung mga problema po ng mga bata pag-ating sa pagtuto.

asr-001733
02:00:34.460 --> 02:00:41.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So may I ask, Secretary, or baka si Yusek Cabral might want to be the one to answer,

asr-001734
02:00:42.600 --> 02:00:47.320
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the huge jump in the budget, sir, kayo yun diba? Kayo yun sa feeding program, right?

asr-001735
02:00:47.480 --> 02:00:48.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, si Asik Roger po.

asr-001736
02:00:48.740 --> 02:00:50.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ah, si Asik Roger pala yun.

asr-001737
02:00:51.260 --> 02:00:53.360
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sorry, medyo magkalupalay kasi na konti.

asr-001738
02:00:53.720 --> 02:00:54.760
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sorry, Yusek Cabral.

asr-001739
02:00:55.760 --> 02:00:57.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Asik Roger, you may ano?

asr-001740
02:00:57.200 --> 02:01:00.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Pwede kayong sumingit dito kung gusto nyo kay Yusek Ron, if you wish to answer.

asr-001741
02:01:01.420 --> 02:01:04.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: May I know, what were the biggest challenges?

asr-001742
02:01:04.420 --> 02:01:09.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi ang laki po ng jump ng pondo in 2026 sa feeding program.

asr-001743
02:01:10.500 --> 02:01:16.040
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Were you able to properly absorb it, distribute the nutritious food?

asr-001744
02:01:18.660 --> 02:01:20.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Para lang guided po kami.

asr-001745
02:01:20.180 --> 02:01:26.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi ako, personally, sasabihin ko right now, intention ko talaga to really push for the increase.

asr-001746
02:01:26.000 --> 02:01:27.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Especially that we have the...

asr-001747
02:01:27.200 --> 02:01:33.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: the Expanded National Nutrition Program or yung Librim Pagkain para sa Batang Pilipino Act in the works.

asr-001748
02:01:33.600 --> 02:01:34.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: In fact, it's almost done.

asr-001749
02:01:35.620 --> 02:01:37.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Nasa BICAM stage na po ito.

asr-001750
02:01:37.680 --> 02:01:39.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, could you help us, Asik Roger?

asr-001751
02:01:40.120 --> 02:01:43.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung naging malaking talon sa pondo ngayong taon,

asr-001752
02:01:44.180 --> 02:01:50.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: were you able to successfully implement the feeding program as stated in the GAA?

asr-001753
02:01:50.740 --> 02:01:56.740
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi sa GAA po, Universal K, Universal Grade 1 at 23 pesos.

asr-001754
02:01:57.200 --> 02:01:58.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 25 pesos.

asr-001755
02:01:59.660 --> 02:02:01.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Were we able to implement that this year?

asr-001756
02:02:01.780 --> 02:02:03.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I see that we have gains eh, diba?

asr-001757
02:02:03.460 --> 02:02:06.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, I'm sure there's a level of implementation we were able to do.

asr-001758
02:02:06.580 --> 02:02:08.660
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But, could you help us, Asik Roger?

asr-001759
02:02:08.940 --> 02:02:11.400
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yes po. Good morning po, Mr. Chair.

asr-001760
02:02:13.300 --> 02:02:14.260
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Allocated na po siya.

asr-001761
02:02:14.540 --> 02:02:18.940
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Tapos, ang kaibahan po ngayon is that nasa division office na po yung pera.

asr-001762
02:02:19.800 --> 02:02:23.900
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, kung mayroon tayong 220 na kabayo, lahat na po ito tumatakbo ngayon.

asr-001763
02:02:23.900 --> 02:02:27.040
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, lahat na po ng division ay nag-iimplementa po.

asr-001764
02:02:27.200 --> 02:02:28.800
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Ng feeding program.

asr-001765
02:02:28.940 --> 02:02:30.420
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Pero, different po yung phasing nila.

asr-001766
02:02:30.560 --> 02:02:31.860
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kasi may naon ang nag-procure.

asr-001767
02:02:32.480 --> 02:02:33.900
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Mayroong nahuli ng konti.

asr-001768
02:02:34.040 --> 02:02:36.100
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Pero, lahat na po sila tumatakbo.

asr-001769
02:02:36.200 --> 02:02:38.220
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yung difference po ngayon, Mr. Chair,

asr-001770
02:02:38.320 --> 02:02:42.960
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: kasi mayroon, may ringgan mo kami ng 1 billion for the central kitchen.

asr-001771
02:02:43.680 --> 02:02:45.280
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, ito po ay for ano na po?

asr-001772
02:02:45.380 --> 02:02:46.880
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: For downloading na po yung pondo.

asr-001773
02:02:47.220 --> 02:02:49.960
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kasi na-approve na po yung design no, yung central kitchen.

asr-001774
02:02:49.960 --> 02:02:53.560
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, more than 200 central kitchen po ang i-build natin ngayon.

asr-001775
02:02:54.220 --> 02:02:57.020
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: That will increase our provision of ano po?

asr-001776
02:02:57.200 --> 02:02:58.680
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Of hot meals.

asr-001777
02:02:59.720 --> 02:03:04.300
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, lahat na po ay nag-iimplementa ng universal kinder, saka universal grade 1.

asr-001778
02:03:04.880 --> 02:03:08.720
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: And then, including po yung mga pregnant mothers, pregnant learners,

asr-001779
02:03:08.880 --> 02:03:12.260
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: saka yung young mothers also na nasa high school.

asr-001780
02:03:12.380 --> 02:03:16.900
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, for the record, Asik Roger, lahat ng skulahan ng DepEd

asr-001781
02:03:16.900 --> 02:03:19.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: nag-iimplement ng universal kinder at grade 1 ngayon.

asr-001782
02:03:19.940 --> 02:03:20.380
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yes, po.

asr-001783
02:03:20.700 --> 02:03:20.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes.

asr-001784
02:03:22.420 --> 02:03:25.800
