Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, because they reduced it to 11 for this year, no?

asr-002100
02:14:18.960 --> 02:14:21.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, how does that...

asr-002101
02:14:24.960 --> 02:14:26.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, they would justify...

asr-002102
02:14:26.960 --> 02:14:27.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Paramo.

asr-002103
02:14:27.960 --> 02:14:30.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, so far, they've only spent 3.5 billion of the 25 billion.

asr-002104
02:14:30.960 --> 02:14:33.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And it's the last quarter already.

asr-002105
02:14:33.960 --> 02:14:36.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But the billing is in the middle of the year, Your Honor.

asr-002106
02:14:36.960 --> 02:14:37.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

asr-002107
02:14:37.960 --> 02:14:38.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, it's related to the school year.

asr-002108
02:14:38.960 --> 02:14:40.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay. Until next year.

asr-002109
02:14:40.960 --> 02:14:42.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: These funds will cross over to next year, Your Honor.

asr-002110
02:14:42.960 --> 02:14:56.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes. Now, at the rate you're going, you are confident that the 25 billion will be fully utilized. Is that right?

asr-002111
02:14:56.960 --> 02:14:57.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-002112
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:04.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Last year, we had the 90% obligation rate, Your Honor.

asr-002113
02:15:04.100 --> 02:15:07.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we're quite confident that we'll be able to spend the money, Your Honor.

asr-002114
02:15:08.020 --> 02:15:10.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: No, but last year, you had 11 billion.

asr-002115
02:15:10.800 --> 02:15:11.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah.

asr-002116
02:15:11.500 --> 02:15:15.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, well, the reason why I'm asking that is,

asr-002117
02:15:16.040 --> 02:15:21.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: if we reduce it for next year, how many will go hungry?

asr-002118
02:15:22.660 --> 02:15:25.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean, you know, I'd like to see the...

asr-002119
02:15:25.400 --> 02:15:26.040
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Beneficiaries.

asr-002120
02:15:26.040 --> 02:15:28.840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, it's a shorter feeding cycle, Your Honor.

asr-002121
02:15:28.840 --> 02:15:32.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, compared to the full school year, you're down to 120 days.

asr-002122
02:15:33.520 --> 02:15:38.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And the observation there is, very successful ka for 120 days,

asr-002123
02:15:38.520 --> 02:15:40.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: but for the remaining days that you don't feed,

asr-002124
02:15:40.960 --> 02:15:44.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: dun bumabalik sa lumang timbang o sa dating timbang yung bata.

asr-002125
02:15:44.260 --> 02:15:46.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay. I'd like that clarified.

asr-002126
02:15:48.660 --> 02:15:51.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we reduced it to 120.

asr-002127
02:15:53.300 --> 02:15:56.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: For this year, it should be, it's 200, right?

asr-002128
02:15:56.240 --> 02:15:58.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's the full school year, 200.

asr-002129
02:15:58.840 --> 02:16:00.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, why did we reduce it?

asr-002130
02:16:00.920 --> 02:16:01.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hindi po.

asr-002131
02:16:01.660 --> 02:16:04.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yung proposal namin ho is for 200,

asr-002132
02:16:04.480 --> 02:16:09.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: but I think it's just a procedure where really it's the NEP level that's restored.

asr-002133
02:16:10.200 --> 02:16:11.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And any congressional insertions,

asr-002134
02:16:12.500 --> 02:16:16.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: alam po nila ni Sen Win as former chair of finance,

asr-002135
02:16:16.720 --> 02:16:18.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they just go back to the NEP level,

asr-002136
02:16:18.400 --> 02:16:25.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and there siguro ang hope there or ang expectation is that Congress will make the same insertion,

asr-002137
02:16:25.320 --> 02:16:27.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which may or may not happen, Your Honor.

asr-002138
02:16:27.100 --> 02:16:27.460
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Which?

asr-002139
02:16:28.840 --> 02:16:35.480
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Which places the burden on us when it should have been in the NEP.

asr-002140
02:16:36.120 --> 02:16:36.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

asr-002141
02:16:36.520 --> 02:16:39.880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang kaya nga namin ilagay, kasi nga yun ang kailangan eh.

asr-002142
02:16:40.580 --> 02:16:42.340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos babalik natin sa NEP.

asr-002143
02:16:42.480 --> 02:16:43.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang ano ba ito?

asr-002144
02:16:43.720 --> 02:16:47.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang, well, well, you know, they have the reasons.

asr-002145
02:16:47.460 --> 02:16:50.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Obviously, fiscal space is tight, et cetera.

asr-002146
02:16:50.600 --> 02:16:56.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But medyo malaking problema yung binaba mo, binalik mo sa 120 days

asr-002147
02:16:56.120 --> 02:16:57.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: because based on your data,

asr-002148
02:16:58.840 --> 02:17:04.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: parang talagang vacation drop, di ba?

asr-002149
02:17:06.460 --> 02:17:11.020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang lahat mong ginawa mo, pinondohan mo, nawawala dahil kulang.

asr-002150
02:17:12.560 --> 02:17:12.740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

asr-002151
02:17:12.820 --> 02:17:14.500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And that was already 200 days, no?

asr-002152
02:17:15.300 --> 02:17:18.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Your latest data was already at 200 days, right?

asr-002153
02:17:19.740 --> 02:17:20.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Is that correct?

asr-002154
02:17:21.180 --> 02:17:22.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: O hindi pa?

asr-002155
02:17:22.360 --> 02:17:23.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 180 yata last year, ho.

asr-002156
02:17:23.920 --> 02:17:24.780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: O yun, 180.

asr-002157
02:17:26.120 --> 02:17:28.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, yun nga, miss.

asr-002158
02:17:28.140 --> 02:17:30.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Bumaba, tapos umakyat.

asr-002159
02:17:30.480 --> 02:17:30.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

asr-002160
02:17:30.820 --> 02:17:31.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Where is that data?

asr-002161
02:17:31.780 --> 02:17:32.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What slide is that?

asr-002162
02:17:34.060 --> 02:17:34.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ah, here.

asr-002163
02:17:35.300 --> 02:17:44.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 42.53%, bumaba, 75, bumaba sa 33, from 24 to 25.

asr-002164
02:17:44.640 --> 02:17:48.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Tapos pagdating ng 25, 26, tumaas na naman, 47.

asr-002165
02:17:48.960 --> 02:17:49.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

asr-002166
02:17:49.520 --> 02:17:50.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-002167
02:17:51.160 --> 02:17:54.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, yung gap na yun, and this is 180 days, correct?

asr-002168
02:17:55.720 --> 02:17:56.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-002169
02:17:56.440 --> 02:17:57.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, can you imagine if it's...

asr-002170
02:17:58.140 --> 02:18:00.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We'll go back to 120 days.

asr-002171
02:18:00.880 --> 02:18:04.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's like, parang ano to?

asr-002172
02:18:04.840 --> 02:18:11.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang nakita na natin yung gap, nakita na natin bumabagsak pa rin at 180 days,

asr-002173
02:18:11.500 --> 02:18:13.900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: pero pinipilit natin yung 120, ah.

asr-002174
02:18:14.340 --> 02:18:15.720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Parang ano ba ito?

asr-002175
02:18:15.860 --> 02:18:22.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Are we trying to solve the problem or are we just churning out numbers for the heck of it?

asr-002176
02:18:22.900 --> 02:18:23.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Di ba?

asr-002177
02:18:23.000 --> 02:18:27.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And for us to be able to put together, what?

asr-002178
02:18:27.660 --> 02:18:28.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Remedies.

asr-002179
02:18:28.860 --> 02:18:33.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But anyway, so obviously, we have to go back to 200 days.

asr-002180
02:18:33.640 --> 02:18:35.520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean, that's the...

asr-002181
02:18:35.520 --> 02:18:37.160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kahit 180, I think, is adequate.

asr-002182
02:18:37.300 --> 02:18:40.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi, Your Honor, sa umpisa ng school year, tinitimbang yun.

asr-002183
02:18:40.500 --> 02:18:42.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, hindi ka nagpapakain sa day one, eh.

asr-002184
02:18:42.880 --> 02:18:44.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, 180, I think, is more than enough.

asr-002185
02:18:45.260 --> 02:18:45.920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay, okay.

asr-002186
02:18:46.300 --> 02:18:51.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Now, on the matter of your...

asr-002187
02:18:51.660 --> 02:18:57.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, maybe you can prepare for plenary because I'll raise this again.

asr-002188
02:18:57.660 --> 02:19:03.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What is the impact of the reduction from 25 billion to 11 billion?

asr-002189
02:19:03.620 --> 02:19:04.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How will this...

asr-002190
02:19:04.660 --> 02:19:06.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You don't have to answer it now because...

asr-002191
02:19:06.040 --> 02:19:06.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-002192
02:19:07.820 --> 02:19:08.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That.

asr-002193
02:19:08.920 --> 02:19:13.760
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Plus, prepare for plenary, the question of...

asr-002194
02:19:13.760 --> 02:19:17.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Well, the Sagipsaka implementation because it turns out...

asr-002195
02:19:21.660 --> 02:19:23.080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Maliit ang percentage, no?

asr-002196
02:19:23.780 --> 02:19:24.700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Noong...

asr-002197
02:19:24.700 --> 02:19:27.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Where is that?

asr-002198
02:19:27.660 --> 02:19:37.120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 0.3% of your purchases for food in the school-based feeding program.

asr-002199
02:19:37.960 --> 02:19:41.040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 0.3% lang ang napunta doon sa Sagipsaka.

asr-002200
02:19:41.260 --> 02:19:43.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah, 35.2 million, Your Honor.

asr-002201
02:19:43.380 --> 02:19:45.420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, of your 25 billion.

asr-002202
02:19:46.320 --> 02:19:48.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Of course, you know, it's staggered.

asr-002203
02:19:48.680 --> 02:19:51.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But why is it small?

asr-002204
02:19:51.620 --> 02:19:52.660
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What are the gaps?

asr-002205
02:19:52.920 --> 02:19:54.140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What do you intend to do?

asr-002206
02:19:54.140 --> 02:19:57.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: How do you intend to bring this forward?

asr-002207
02:19:57.660 --> 02:20:01.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And, again, in plenary, you can answer that.

asr-002208
02:20:01.580 --> 02:20:06.220
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But if you have initial comments or, you know...

asr-002209
02:20:06.220 --> 02:20:10.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: With your permission, I'll ask Asik Roger to explain that.

asr-002210
02:20:10.040 --> 02:20:10.640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Go ahead, sir.

asr-002211
02:20:11.800 --> 02:20:12.100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Roger.

asr-002212
02:20:13.940 --> 02:20:14.580
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yes, sir.

asr-002213
02:20:15.880 --> 02:20:27.420
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Bali po, five provinces and four provinces and one city po ang gumamit po ng modality ng procurement on Sagipsaka.

asr-002214
02:20:27.660 --> 02:20:35.380
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Which is the Cauyan City, Zamboanga del Sur, Sulu Province, General Santo City, and then Sorigao del Sur.

asr-002215
02:20:36.460 --> 02:20:43.840
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Amounting to 35.2 million po yung cost nung ginamit po sa Sagipsaka.

asr-002216
02:20:44.020 --> 02:20:47.540
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Which is very small. Medyo, ano po, mababa po talaga.

asr-002217
02:20:47.700 --> 02:20:47.940
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yes.

asr-002218
02:20:47.940 --> 02:20:56.420
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Pero po, nagkandak na po kami ng mga orientation po sa ating mga school-based feeding coordinator sa buong bansa.

asr-002219
02:20:57.040 --> 02:20:57.540
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: At...

asr-002220
02:20:57.540 --> 02:21:08.620
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: We are trying to prepare, Mr. Chair, ng manual or guidelines on how to implement SBFP sa true Sagipsaka.

asr-002221
02:21:09.560 --> 02:21:14.460
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Para po, mas dumami po yung mag-implement nito.

asr-002222
02:21:14.460 --> 02:21:23.440
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: And then, ang nakuha po naming information, Mr. Chair, yung mga individual farmers natin, small farmers,

asr-002223
02:21:23.660 --> 02:21:27.460
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: ay medyo nahirapan mag-register po sa

asr-002224
02:21:27.540 --> 02:21:29.540
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: FIDES system.

asr-002225
02:21:30.300 --> 02:21:35.220
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kaya hindi po sila makasali sa procurement.

asr-002226
02:21:36.160 --> 02:21:41.940
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kaya mas maganda po na ma-organize po talaga into cooperatives yung ating mga small farmers.

asr-002227
02:21:42.360 --> 02:21:46.640
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Para mayroon po silang scale na sumali sa...

asr-002228
02:21:46.640 --> 02:21:51.140
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kasi po, pag nag-procure ka po ng feeding, it's the entire year na po.

asr-002229
02:21:51.640 --> 02:21:51.980
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Yes.

asr-002230
02:21:52.120 --> 02:21:56.940
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: Kung hindi po consistent yung ani niya, parang mahirapan po siyang manalo doon sa...

asr-002231
02:21:57.540 --> 02:21:59.020
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: sa procurement.

asr-002232
02:21:59.240 --> 02:22:04.040
DepEd Assistant Secretary Roger B. Masapol: So, kung ano po, kung organized po talaga sila, mas malaki po yung chances po, Mr. Chair.

asr-002233
02:22:04.340 --> 02:22:07.580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Although, I think, well, maybe you can be flexible, no?

asr-002234
02:22:07.640 --> 02:22:11.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasi, before they get organized, it will take time.

asr-002235
02:22:11.680 --> 02:22:18.380
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Habang nandiyan yung produkto nila, nandiyan yung ani nila, na pag hindi binili, itatapon.

asr-002236
02:22:18.700 --> 02:22:18.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know?

asr-002237
02:22:19.200 --> 02:22:22.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, baka kailangan merong flexibility para...

asr-002238
02:22:22.540 --> 02:22:26.540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: As we work towards the ideal, because...

asr-002239
02:22:26.540 --> 02:22:27.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You know?

asr-002240
02:22:27.540 --> 02:22:33.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: We've already passed here in the Senate yung Bureau of Agriculture and Fisheries Co-ops re-establishment, no?

asr-002241
02:22:34.060 --> 02:22:35.400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, that will take time.

asr-002242
02:22:35.780 --> 02:22:37.280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, maybe you can put...

asr-002243
02:22:37.280 --> 02:22:45.800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And if you can submit to us yung sinasabing yung mahirap mag-register sa DA, no?

asr-002244
02:22:45.860 --> 02:22:49.060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because that shouldn't be a hurdle, no?

asr-002245
02:22:49.700 --> 02:22:52.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat madali mag-register sa DA, no?

asr-002246
02:22:52.600 --> 02:22:56.240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, if you can give that to us, then we will work on that.

asr-002247
02:22:56.420 --> 02:22:57.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We'll do that, Your Honor.

asr-002248
02:22:57.540 --> 02:23:00.160
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, and yeah, I hope.

asr-002249
02:23:00.820 --> 02:23:07.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I'd like to think, in fairness, the implementation of the Sagipsaka program for your feeding program,

asr-002250
02:23:08.100 --> 02:23:15.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: dahil nag-umpisa ang pasokan ng August, doon lang, by and large, di ba, yung pag-iimplementa,

asr-002251
02:23:15.880 --> 02:23:19.200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: nag-umpisa rin about a couple of months ago, three months ago.

asr-002252
02:23:19.780 --> 02:23:27.260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And so, you're really still in the initial stages of being able to implement the program and the law.

asr-002253
02:23:27.540 --> 02:23:29.860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, we'll grant you that.

asr-002254
02:23:29.980 --> 02:23:36.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But we'd like to, during plenary, just submit to us, how do you intend to fully implement this?

asr-002255
02:23:36.900 --> 02:23:38.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What are the challenges?

asr-002256
02:23:38.400 --> 02:23:41.680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: What do we have to address on the supply side?

asr-002257
02:23:42.780 --> 02:23:44.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The demand side, walang problema eh.

asr-002258
02:23:45.440 --> 02:23:49.300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yung supply side, I'm sure you're also going to have a lot of challenges there.

asr-002259
02:23:49.680 --> 02:23:52.360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And we'd like to address both.

asr-002260
02:23:52.360 --> 02:23:56.600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: In the end, you're going to have fresh produce.

asr-002261
02:23:57.540 --> 02:24:02.000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sariwang pagkain, you'd like to move away from the, what is the term?

asr-002262
02:24:02.900 --> 02:24:06.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: NFP to hot meals, di ba?

asr-002263
02:24:07.640 --> 02:24:12.960
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And I know for a fact that many of your school children look forward to the hot meals.

asr-002264
02:24:14.140 --> 02:24:19.620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's a plus, an incentive for them to go to school.

asr-002265
02:24:19.620 --> 02:24:27.320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And therefore, moving towards that direction will not just ensure better quality.

asr-002266
02:24:27.540 --> 02:24:32.820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That quality education for our children, it will also help our farmers and our fisher folks.

asr-002267
02:24:32.900 --> 02:24:37.940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, you're really having one fund, but two beneficiaries.

asr-002268
02:24:39.200 --> 02:24:42.840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Which is how government spending should be, di ba?

asr-002269
02:24:42.840 --> 02:24:52.440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: One expenditure, but several outcomes and several outcomes, yes.

asr-002270
02:24:53.600 --> 02:24:55.680
