asr-005789
04:36:22.120 --> 04:36:24.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: with your permission.

asr-005790
04:36:24.120 --> 04:36:26.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Asek, maybe first question.

asr-005791
04:36:26.120 --> 04:36:27.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is it 20% nga ba?

asr-005792
04:36:27.120 --> 04:36:30.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: 20% nga ba ng mga studyante merong special needs?

asr-005793
04:36:30.120 --> 04:36:32.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Mr. Chair, good afternoon po.

asr-005794
04:36:32.120 --> 04:36:35.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: As I remember, it is a result of a study

asr-005795
04:36:35.120 --> 04:36:37.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: of the youth impact.

asr-005796
04:36:37.120 --> 04:36:40.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: So, unverified siya in the field,

asr-005797
04:36:40.120 --> 04:36:42.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: but, based on our LIS,

asr-005798
04:36:42.120 --> 04:36:45.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: ang confirmed po yung natag pong studyante

asr-005799
04:36:45.120 --> 04:36:49.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: is around 495,000

asr-005800
04:36:49.120 --> 04:36:51.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: and only 100,000,

asr-005801
04:36:51.120 --> 04:36:54.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: around 150,000 of them

asr-005802
04:36:54.120 --> 04:36:56.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: have medical diagnosis.

asr-005803
04:36:56.120 --> 04:36:58.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. So, I know that diagnosis is also a problem

asr-005804
04:36:58.120 --> 04:37:00.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kasi mahal magpa-diagnose.

asr-005805
04:37:00.120 --> 04:37:05.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, let's say 400 yung suspected na merong special needs.

asr-005806
04:37:05.120 --> 04:37:07.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that fair to say?

asr-005807
04:37:07.120 --> 04:37:08.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Yes po.

asr-005808
04:37:08.120 --> 04:37:10.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay. Kung 400,000 yan,

asr-005809
04:37:10.120 --> 04:37:13.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: that's about 2%, no?

asr-005810
04:37:13.120 --> 04:37:15.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Or less than,

asr-005811
04:37:15.120 --> 04:37:18.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: yeah, less than 2%.

asr-005812
04:37:18.120 --> 04:37:20.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, and again, this is not for this year's,

asr-005813
04:37:20.120 --> 04:37:22.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: not for right now,

asr-005814
04:37:22.120 --> 04:37:24.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but maybe for the plenary.

asr-005815
04:37:24.120 --> 04:37:26.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: If you can help us understand,

asr-005816
04:37:26.120 --> 04:37:28.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ilan ba talaga yung mga bata

asr-005817
04:37:28.120 --> 04:37:30.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: na nangangailangan ng special care

asr-005818
04:37:30.120 --> 04:37:32.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: and special education,

asr-005819
04:37:32.120 --> 04:37:34.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: that will be a very important starting point

asr-005820
04:37:34.120 --> 04:37:35.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kasi from there,

asr-005821
04:37:35.120 --> 04:37:38.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: pwede natin matrack yung pangangailangan nila

asr-005822
04:37:38.120 --> 04:37:41.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: across the system, no?

asr-005823
04:37:41.120 --> 04:37:44.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Sa ILRC, it's funded,

asr-005824
04:37:44.120 --> 04:37:46.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it's legislated,

asr-005825
04:37:46.120 --> 04:37:48.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but what more can we do?

asr-005826
04:37:48.120 --> 04:37:49.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung diagnosis, I know,

asr-005827
04:37:49.120 --> 04:37:51.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: is a current issue

asr-005828
04:37:51.120 --> 04:37:53.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: because there's not enough individuals

asr-005829
04:37:53.120 --> 04:37:54.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: who can diagnose

asr-005830
04:37:54.120 --> 04:37:57.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: at alam ko mamahalin yung diagnosis.

asr-005831
04:37:57.120 --> 04:37:58.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's one.

asr-005832
04:37:58.120 --> 04:38:00.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And then yung teachers, of course,

asr-005833
04:38:00.120 --> 04:38:02.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think we talked about this earlier

asr-005834
04:38:02.120 --> 04:38:04.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: with other senators,

asr-005835
04:38:04.120 --> 04:38:06.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but in the case na hindi mo kayang

asr-005836
04:38:06.120 --> 04:38:11.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: makomplement ng lahat ng klase ng teachers,

asr-005837
04:38:11.120 --> 04:38:14.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: do we have SNED teachers,

asr-005838
04:38:14.120 --> 04:38:17.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: at least the basic SNED teachers

asr-005839
04:38:17.120 --> 04:38:18.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: for these facilities?

asr-005840
04:38:18.120 --> 04:38:23.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Asec?

asr-005841
04:38:23.120 --> 04:38:24.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: At this time po,

asr-005842
04:38:24.120 --> 04:38:25.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: we only have in our data

asr-005843
04:38:25.120 --> 04:38:27.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: 6,000 plus SNED teachers

asr-005844
04:38:27.120 --> 04:38:29.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: na under that plantelia,

asr-005845
04:38:29.120 --> 04:38:30.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: specific plantelia.

asr-005846
04:38:30.120 --> 04:38:32.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Pero meron po tayong undergoing training

asr-005847
04:38:32.120 --> 04:38:34.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: on receiving teachers.

asr-005848
04:38:34.120 --> 04:38:35.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: In the inclusive education,

asr-005849
04:38:35.120 --> 04:38:39.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: ang trend po ay kahit general education practitioner

asr-005850
04:38:39.120 --> 04:38:41.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: would be able to cater to special needs.

asr-005851
04:38:41.120 --> 04:38:42.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: With a little training,

asr-005852
04:38:42.120 --> 04:38:44.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: with a little bit more training, no?

asr-005853
04:38:44.120 --> 04:38:48.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, so dun sa 400,000,

asr-005854
04:38:48.120 --> 04:38:51.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: suspected or we're assuming

asr-005855
04:38:51.120 --> 04:38:53.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: na they're special needs children,

asr-005856
04:38:53.120 --> 04:38:56.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ilang guro yung kailangan nila?

asr-005857
04:38:56.120 --> 04:38:58.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung total na kailangan nilang guro?

asr-005858
04:38:58.120 --> 04:39:00.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Sa inclusive education principle po,

asr-005859
04:39:00.120 --> 04:39:04.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: based on our SNED forum conducted two weeks ago,

asr-005860
04:39:04.120 --> 04:39:06.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: ang tinitignan po natin ay sa mainstreaming

asr-005861
04:39:06.120 --> 04:39:09.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: when we include our special learners,

asr-005862
04:39:09.120 --> 04:39:11.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: at least we have one receiving teacher

asr-005863
04:39:11.120 --> 04:39:14.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: for every five, ideally.

asr-005864
04:39:14.120 --> 04:39:17.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So that's 80,000 teachers?

asr-005865
04:39:17.120 --> 04:39:19.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kung 400,000?

asr-005866
04:39:19.120 --> 04:39:20.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Most likely.

asr-005867
04:39:20.120 --> 04:39:22.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, and we only have 6,000 teachers right now.

asr-005868
04:39:22.120 --> 04:39:23.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yeah.

asr-005869
04:39:23.120 --> 04:39:24.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Okay.

asr-005870
04:39:24.120 --> 04:39:26.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: But just to clarify,

asr-005871
04:39:26.120 --> 04:39:29.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: na we don't really need the specialized teachers

asr-005872
04:39:29.120 --> 04:39:31.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: because we will not have that one.

asr-005873
04:39:31.120 --> 04:39:34.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: So we need to train our teachers

asr-005874
04:39:34.120 --> 04:39:36.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: to be receiving teachers

asr-005875
04:39:36.120 --> 04:39:37.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: for the inclusive education.

asr-005876
04:39:37.120 --> 04:39:38.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Okay.

asr-005877
04:39:38.120 --> 04:39:39.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So roughly,

asr-005878
04:39:39.120 --> 04:39:41.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: whether they're formally trained

asr-005879
04:39:41.120 --> 04:39:42.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or they're a receiving teacher,

asr-005880
04:39:42.120 --> 04:39:43.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: we need about 80,000 of them.

asr-005881
04:39:43.120 --> 04:39:44.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Correct, no?

asr-005882
04:39:44.120 --> 04:39:45.120
DepEd Assistant Secretary Romeo T. Benviaje: Opo.

asr-005883
04:39:45.120 --> 04:39:46.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: To, to fulfill the ratio of

asr-005884
04:39:46.120 --> 04:39:48.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: one is to five.

asr-005885
04:39:48.120 --> 04:39:51.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Well, ang ratio natin in Baguio, for example,

asr-005886
04:39:51.120 --> 04:39:54.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: is one is to 3,700.

asr-005887
04:39:54.120 --> 04:39:57.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ang ratio in Malabon is one is to 3,000.

asr-005888
04:39:57.120 --> 04:40:00.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Tarlac is doing better at one is to 1,200.

asr-005889
04:40:00.120 --> 04:40:04.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So one is to five is a huge jump from where we are.

asr-005890
04:40:04.120 --> 04:40:07.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But we're committed, ASEC, no?

asr-005891
04:40:07.120 --> 04:40:09.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We're committed to support this.

asr-005892
04:40:09.120 --> 04:40:11.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Anyway, there's a separate legislation for this.

asr-005893
04:40:11.120 --> 04:40:13.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So it's not like we have a choice.

asr-005894
04:40:13.120 --> 04:40:14.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We really have to push it.

asr-005895
04:40:14.120 --> 04:40:15.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: At sabi nga ho namin,

asr-005896
04:40:15.120 --> 04:40:17.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: yung mga special needs ng mga kabataan,

asr-005897
04:40:17.120 --> 04:40:20.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kailangan talaga ng special na tulong.

asr-005898
04:40:20.120 --> 04:40:24.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And we need to provide more resources for them, no?

asr-005899
04:40:24.120 --> 04:40:27.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So request ko po for the plenary.

asr-005900
04:40:27.120 --> 04:40:29.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Number one, help us understand the numbers.

asr-005901
04:40:29.120 --> 04:40:33.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi yung 2% to 20% ang laki ng gap.

asr-005902
04:40:33.120 --> 04:40:34.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Ang laki ng jump na yan.

asr-005903
04:40:34.120 --> 04:40:37.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And I understand that 20% is an unverified study.

asr-005904
04:40:37.120 --> 04:40:40.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: But you would be in a good position to tell us,

asr-005905
04:40:40.120 --> 04:40:41.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: ilan ba talaga yan?

asr-005906
04:40:41.120 --> 04:40:43.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Huwag muna natin bilangin yung diagnosed

asr-005907
04:40:43.120 --> 04:40:45.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: because alam natin na maraming

asr-005908
04:40:45.120 --> 04:40:46.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: left undiagnosed.

asr-005909
04:40:46.120 --> 04:40:48.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So even yung sa tingin natin,

asr-005910
04:40:48.120 --> 04:40:50.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: baka may pangailangang special,

asr-005911
04:40:50.120 --> 04:40:52.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: i-note nyo na rin.

asr-005912
04:40:52.120 --> 04:40:54.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Tell us before the plenary kung ilan yan.

asr-005913
04:40:54.120 --> 04:40:56.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And then tell us the ratio.

asr-005914
04:40:56.120 --> 04:41:00.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Do I take it correctly na more than the facilities,

asr-005915
04:41:00.120 --> 04:41:03.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: more than the paraphernalia and the equipment,

asr-005916
04:41:03.120 --> 04:41:06.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it's really the teachers that we need to focus on?

asr-005917
04:41:08.120 --> 04:41:10.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's the teachers, Mr. President.

asr-005918
04:41:10.120 --> 04:41:12.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But it's also the access to development pediatricians

asr-005919
04:41:12.120 --> 04:41:14.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: because it's a development pediatrician

asr-005920
04:41:14.120 --> 04:41:18.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: who can accurately diagnose the learning deficiency

asr-005921
04:41:18.120 --> 04:41:21.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and prescribe whether that child is best included

asr-005922
04:41:21.120 --> 04:41:24.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: with the larger class or best left to a one-to-one

asr-005923
04:41:24.120 --> 04:41:27.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: or one-is-to-two special class.

asr-005924
04:41:27.120 --> 04:41:29.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We've had discussions about this.

asr-005925
04:41:29.120 --> 04:41:31.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yun ang talagang, that intervention is missing.

asr-005926
04:41:31.120 --> 04:41:34.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So I said earlier, what's promising is what,

asr-005927
04:41:34.120 --> 04:41:38.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I know Dr. Yi is talking to Dr. Ho of PhilHealth.

asr-005928
04:41:38.120 --> 04:41:42.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So what they're doing and talking to the medical association

asr-005929
04:41:42.120 --> 04:41:43.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: is very promising.

asr-005930
04:41:43.120 --> 04:41:45.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think that one is an immediate solution

asr-005931
04:41:45.120 --> 04:41:49.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: rather than trying to reach for nirvana

asr-005932
04:41:49.120 --> 04:41:53.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: under the ILRC law which is probably decades away

asr-005933
04:41:53.120 --> 04:41:56.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: given the budgetary requirements.

asr-005934
04:41:56.120 --> 04:41:59.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's something that we can do tomorrow or next week.

asr-005935
04:41:59.120 --> 04:42:03.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary, before I give the floor to Senator Joel,

asr-005936
04:42:03.120 --> 04:42:05.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: yes, we will have the funding,

asr-005937
04:42:05.120 --> 04:42:10.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: but we don't have enough of the developmental pediatricians

asr-005938
04:42:10.120 --> 04:42:11.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: nor their time.

asr-005939
04:42:11.120 --> 04:42:12.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We don't have enough in the country, Mr. President.

asr-005940
04:42:12.120 --> 04:42:13.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Exactly.

asr-005941
04:42:13.120 --> 04:42:15.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So kahit may pondo tayo sa PhilHealth,

asr-005942
04:42:15.120 --> 04:42:17.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: If you try to make an appointment for your child,

asr-005943
04:42:17.120 --> 04:42:19.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: it will take you at least a year to get an appointment.

asr-005944
04:42:19.120 --> 04:42:22.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Let me ask Senator Joel who has personal experience here.

asr-005945
04:42:22.120 --> 04:42:25.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: I was about to butt in, Mr. Chairman,

asr-005946
04:42:25.120 --> 04:42:33.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: because I'm a father of a special kid, Mr. Chairman,

asr-005947
04:42:33.120 --> 04:42:41.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: and it pains a lot because last time I visited Minuyan Elementary School

asr-005948
04:42:41.120 --> 04:42:43.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: in San Jose del Monte,

asr-005949
04:42:43.120 --> 04:42:48.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: and I actually immediately called the attention

asr-005950
04:42:48.120 --> 04:42:50.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: of our good secretary about this

asr-005951
04:42:50.120 --> 04:42:54.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: because when I went to this particular elementary school,

asr-005952
04:42:54.120 --> 04:43:01.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: there are about 140, 150 students with special needs,

asr-005953
04:43:01.120 --> 04:43:05.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: and I asked them how many teachers do they have.

asr-005954
04:43:05.120 --> 04:43:06.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: They only have two.

asr-005955
04:43:06.120 --> 04:43:08.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Actually, they only have two.

asr-005956
04:43:08.120 --> 04:43:11.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I asked them if the students were ready,

asr-005957
04:43:11.120 --> 04:43:13.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: if they were already diagnosed.

asr-005958
04:43:13.120 --> 04:43:19.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And according to her, less than 10 students were diagnosed.

asr-005959
04:43:19.120 --> 04:43:21.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: So this is really alarming,

asr-005960
04:43:21.120 --> 04:43:26.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: and as mentioned by Secretary Angara,

asr-005961
04:43:26.120 --> 04:43:30.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: the biggest problem right now is the development of the pediatrician.

asr-005962
04:43:30.120 --> 04:43:35.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: I personally experienced that when you go to a development pediatrician,

asr-005963
04:43:35.120 --> 04:43:40.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: in my case, I remember there are only two, Mr. Chairman.

asr-005964
04:43:40.120 --> 04:43:41.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: There are only two.

asr-005965
04:43:41.120 --> 04:43:47.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: One is Dr. Dimalanta of St. Luke's and Dr. Lexi Reyes of Makati Med.

asr-005966
04:43:47.120 --> 04:43:53.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And you're not even talking about occupational therapy, speech therapies, etc.

asr-005967
04:43:53.120 --> 04:43:59.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And so even in our discussions with the Committee on Higher and Technical Education,

asr-005968
04:43:59.120 --> 04:44:03.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: we discussed this fully last time during the budget deliberation

asr-005969
04:44:03.120 --> 04:44:06.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: when we were talking about the Dr. Parasabayan,

asr-005970
04:44:06.120 --> 04:44:08.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: the implementation of Dr. Parasabayan,

asr-005971
04:44:08.120 --> 04:44:10.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: which we are in a very good position.

asr-005972
04:44:10.120 --> 04:44:12.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: In a very good position right now.

asr-005973
04:44:12.120 --> 04:44:20.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Before, there are only seven regions na meron pong public school of medicine.

asr-005974
04:44:20.120 --> 04:44:25.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now there are, I mean, all regions have their own.

asr-005975
04:44:25.120 --> 04:44:27.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: What's the number?

asr-005976
04:44:27.120 --> 04:44:34.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: From eight state college universities offering school of medicine,

asr-005977
04:44:34.120 --> 04:44:35.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: now it's 30.

asr-005978
04:44:35.120 --> 04:44:37.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Three zero.

asr-005979
04:44:37.120 --> 04:44:43.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: But when we check as to how many development pediatricians are we producing,

asr-005980
04:44:43.120 --> 04:44:48.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: and we asked the DOH and through the help of EDCOM,

asr-005981
04:44:48.120 --> 04:44:51.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: dalawa lang daw po yung binibigay a year.

asr-005982
04:44:51.120 --> 04:44:58.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And so we were surprised kahit na nag-a-ask sila ng request for several years,

asr-005983
04:44:58.120 --> 04:45:00.120
Senator Joel Villanueva: talagang ang maximum na binibigay.

asr-005984
04:45:00.000 --> 04:45:03.240
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dalawa. Dalawang doktor, Mr. Chairman.

asr-005985
04:45:03.420 --> 04:45:05.660
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, it's really a big problem.

asr-005986
04:45:05.660 --> 04:45:09.640
Senator Joel Villanueva: And when you're talking about the 20%, Sir Yusek, with all due respect,

asr-005987
04:45:09.760 --> 04:45:16.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm not sure of the numbers, how we can actually double-check these figures.

asr-005988
04:45:16.480 --> 04:45:18.480
Senator Joel Villanueva: Because there's a lot. There's a lot.

asr-005989
04:45:18.900 --> 04:45:21.420
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, I hope that we can do something about this.

asr-005990
04:45:21.460 --> 04:45:24.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: This is really personal to me, Mr. Chairman.

asr-005991
04:45:24.580 --> 04:45:26.280
Senator Joel Villanueva: I hope we can do something.

asr-005992
04:45:26.380 --> 04:45:28.820
Senator Joel Villanueva: But we can start with the teachers, of course.

asr-005993
04:45:28.820 --> 04:45:35.820
Senator Joel Villanueva: Because, again, there are so many schools out there na wala rin guru yung SNED at SPED nila.

asr-005994
04:45:35.940 --> 04:45:37.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Senator. Yes, Secretary.

asr-005995
04:45:37.980 --> 04:45:41.140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: With your permission, on the permission of Senator Joel and the Senate President.

asr-005996
04:45:41.920 --> 04:45:46.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The same way we passed the Dr. Parsabay, and I was still in the Senate when we passed that,

asr-005997
04:45:46.640 --> 04:45:52.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: there was talk of passing a law, similar law, for allied health professionals, Your Honor.

asr-005998
04:45:53.320 --> 04:45:56.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Senator Joel, Senator Pia, I remember we were talking about that.

asr-005999
04:45:56.220 --> 04:45:58.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And I think that's worth pursuing, Your Honor.

asr-006000
04:45:58.600 --> 04:46:06.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And maybe look at the School of Health Sciences model of PGH, where the problem is geographic.

asr-006001
04:46:07.360 --> 04:46:11.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: There are many areas that have no takers, no offerers of these courses.

asr-006002
04:46:11.880 --> 04:46:15.740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, you really have no pipeline down the road, Mr. President.

asr-006003
04:46:16.320 --> 04:46:21.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But if you have, similar to the School of Health Sciences of PGH in Tacloban, in Coronadal,

asr-006004
04:46:22.560 --> 04:46:28.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which are not quite getting the attention, but they're, kasi may return service huyon eh.

asr-006005
04:46:28.600 --> 04:46:33.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, you have your STs or speech therapists, your OTs, occupational therapists.

asr-006006
04:46:33.720 --> 04:46:36.080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: You will have them with the requirement to serve for four years.

asr-006007
04:46:36.180 --> 04:46:39.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maaring ma-pirate yon, but they have to serve their four years, Mr. President.

asr-006008
04:46:39.920 --> 04:46:42.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then, you just produce a consistent pipeline.

asr-006009
04:46:42.360 --> 04:46:47.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, it would help to have, if not a law, then a program for allied health professionals, Your Honor.

asr-006010
04:46:48.060 --> 04:46:49.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you, Secretaries.

asr-006011
04:46:49.480 --> 04:46:58.380
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Maybe just to end this point, we know that yung Sned or yung SPED, it used to be called SPED.

asr-006012
04:46:58.600 --> 04:46:59.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yung Sned na yung pangalan.

asr-006013
04:47:00.460 --> 04:47:05.980
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: It's something we've been doing, but we all see that meron talagang gaps.

asr-006014
04:47:06.540 --> 04:47:09.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Whether it's a personal gap, a funding gap.

asr-006015
04:47:11.240 --> 04:47:17.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And I'm hoping that while I'm chairman here, mahanapan natin ito ng solusyon.

asr-006016
04:47:17.800 --> 04:47:20.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And it's not as easy as just putting money.

asr-006017
04:47:20.900 --> 04:47:25.400
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi we know that that solves some problems, but not all problems.

asr-006018
04:47:25.560 --> 04:47:27.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we have actually asked EDCOM to take a further...

asr-006019
04:47:28.600 --> 04:47:36.180
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: look into the way that we provide education for our special needs children.

asr-006020
04:47:36.940 --> 04:47:41.700
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And maybe in preparation for next year's budget or next year's implementation,

asr-006021
04:47:41.900 --> 04:47:48.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: or next next year's budget or implementation, we can take a more detailed look at the numbers.

asr-006022
04:47:48.980 --> 04:47:51.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi currently, EDCOM 2 says 20%.

asr-006023
04:47:51.300 --> 04:47:52.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: You're saying it's 2%.

asr-006024
04:47:52.680 --> 04:47:55.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, dun pa lang, di na tayo nagkaka-agree, di ba?

asr-006025
04:47:55.280 --> 04:47:56.420
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we can look at that.

asr-006026
04:47:56.420 --> 04:47:58.500
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We can look at the pipeline.

asr-006027
04:47:58.500 --> 04:48:02.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We can look at the pipeline of teachers, and EDCOM naman also includes CHED and even TESDA.

asr-006028
04:48:02.560 --> 04:48:06.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, we can look at how we can try to affect that pipeline as well.

asr-006029
04:48:07.060 --> 04:48:13.120
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Then at the proper time, pag panahon na talaga na mapondohan natin ito ng mas maganda at mas maayos,

asr-006030
04:48:13.220 --> 04:48:17.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: kapag malinaw na yung magandang gawin, then I think we can come together for this.

asr-006031
04:48:17.580 --> 04:48:17.880
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary.

asr-006032
04:48:18.720 --> 04:48:19.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-006033
04:48:19.780 --> 04:48:24.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We really appreciate that concern for special needs education.

asr-006034
04:48:24.660 --> 04:48:27.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But perhaps we should also be looking at it alongside universities.

asr-006035
04:48:28.500 --> 04:48:43.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I think that's the impetus really for really all institutions, all possible institutions coming together.

asr-006036
04:48:43.520 --> 04:48:50.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because if DepEd tries to address it in a DepEd fashion with DepEd funding alone, then it will take many decades.

asr-006037
04:48:50.000 --> 04:48:56.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But if all institutions come together to produce the services, it's really a service that's needed.

asr-006038
04:48:57.300 --> 04:48:58.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: An accurate diagnosis.

asr-006039
04:48:58.500 --> 04:49:01.500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, the diagnosis doesn't have to come from a DepEd doctor.

asr-006040
04:49:01.620 --> 04:49:03.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It doesn't have to come, it can come from any doctor.

asr-006041
04:49:04.760 --> 04:49:07.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It just needs someone to pay for that service down the road.

asr-006042
04:49:07.620 --> 04:49:10.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And that public school student definitely does not have the capacity to pay.

asr-006043
04:49:10.980 --> 04:49:17.340
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But because we subscribe to universal healthcare, then there should be a package for these children.

asr-006044
04:49:17.500 --> 04:49:19.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because I think that's the spirit of field.

asr-006045
04:49:19.840 --> 04:49:22.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's to care for the ones who need it the most, Mr. Chair.

asr-006046
04:49:22.580 --> 04:49:23.560
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, I agree.

asr-006047
04:49:23.640 --> 04:49:23.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Secretary.

asr-006048
04:49:23.860 --> 04:49:25.960
Senator Joel Villanueva: May I just, just very short time, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006049
04:49:26.060 --> 04:49:28.300
Senator Joel Villanueva: I agree with what the Secretary mentioned.

asr-006050
04:49:28.500 --> 04:49:29.780
Senator Joel Villanueva: The whole of government approach.

asr-006051
04:49:30.160 --> 04:49:35.060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Unfortunately, for the past so many years, parang walang nag-aasikaso, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006052
04:49:35.180 --> 04:49:40.920
Senator Joel Villanueva: There are low-hanging fruits that we can actually implement right away.

asr-006053
04:49:41.000 --> 04:49:45.580
Senator Joel Villanueva: For example, PCMC, in a year, five lang yung scholars nila, natitrain nila.

asr-006054
04:49:45.800 --> 04:49:48.220
Senator Joel Villanueva: But they can do 15, at least 15.

asr-006055
04:49:48.680 --> 04:49:51.920
Senator Joel Villanueva: NCH, National Children's, eight lang a year.

asr-006056
04:49:52.220 --> 04:49:54.140
Senator Joel Villanueva: PGH, two a year, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006057
04:49:54.300 --> 04:49:57.580
Senator Joel Villanueva: They can do plus 10 at least, plus 10 for NCH.

asr-006058
04:49:58.500 --> 04:50:02.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: But there are only 35 plantilia that we are looking at, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006059
04:50:02.720 --> 04:50:13.620
Senator Joel Villanueva: These are things that we just discovered that we can actually do right away without going through the mills of passing laws, etc.

asr-006060
04:50:13.720 --> 04:50:20.220
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, again, Mr. Chairman, thank you for this opportunity that we were able to tackle this very important topic.

asr-006061
04:50:20.320 --> 04:50:20.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Thank you.

asr-006062
04:50:21.020 --> 04:50:28.020
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And, Secretary, three of the five EDCOM members are here, so we will ask EDCOM to take a special look at this, no?

asr-006063
04:50:28.020 --> 04:50:32.680
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And include PhilHealth, kasi kapag yung PhilHealth, bukas na yung pondo sa kanila,

asr-006064
04:50:32.820 --> 04:50:39.260
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: it might even generate more individuals going into these fields which can specifically cater to the special needs.

asr-006065
04:50:39.260 --> 04:50:41.680
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We agree with you wholeheartedly. Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman.

asr-006066
04:50:41.680 --> 04:50:42.540
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yes, thank you. Thank you for that.

asr-006067
04:50:43.000 --> 04:50:47.280
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay, I have, unless the Senate President has some more points, I have a few more points.

asr-006068
04:50:47.600 --> 04:50:47.860
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Go ahead.

asr-006069
04:50:47.860 --> 04:50:48.140
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Go ahead, okay.

asr-006070
04:50:48.880 --> 04:50:50.300
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: El Nino, okay.

asr-006071
04:50:51.580 --> 04:50:57.960
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: We're assuming that yung tubig mas magiging mahirap in a few months.

asr-006072
04:50:58.080 --> 04:51:04.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I know there are already a hundred plus municipalities who have declared an emergency because of El Nino.

asr-006073
04:51:05.700 --> 04:51:11.200
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Are our schools prepared for a possible shortage of water?

asr-006074
04:51:11.420 --> 04:51:13.220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that something we're looking at, Secretary?

asr-006075
04:51:13.680 --> 04:51:14.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-006076
04:51:15.380 --> 04:51:21.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're looking at rising temperatures, so we want each school, ideally, or each classroom, actually,

asr-006077
04:51:21.820 --> 04:51:26.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: to have a, what they call a jerry can, yung lalagyan ng tubig.

asr-006078
04:51:28.020 --> 04:51:30.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For, so to prevent dehydration, Your Honor.

asr-006079
04:51:30.840 --> 04:51:37.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And of course, in the extreme situations, merong pag tumaman na po ng 40 plus degrees yung temperature,

asr-006080
04:51:37.560 --> 04:51:41.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: then you have to send, really have to send, even before that, you have to send kids home already.

asr-006081
04:51:41.880 --> 04:51:46.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because you'll have headaches, their noses will start bleeding, et cetera.

asr-006082
04:51:47.100 --> 04:51:52.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, to be clear, kapag high temperature, you're going to call off classes?

asr-006083
04:51:52.460 --> 04:51:53.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We may have to, Your Honor.

asr-006084
04:51:53.420 --> 04:51:55.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Is that done at the school level or at the LGU level?

asr-006085
04:51:55.720 --> 04:51:57.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, because that's an emergency.

asr-006086
04:51:58.020 --> 04:52:04.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The school is actually empowered to do that under existing EOs if it reaches emergency levels already, Your Honor.

asr-006087
04:52:04.940 --> 04:52:09.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But generally, it's the LGU who would call off classes, Your Honor.

asr-006088
04:52:09.800 --> 04:52:18.520
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: And, well, gusto ko lang i-flag lang yung lack of water for the CR, for the canteen, drinking water, for hydration.

asr-006089
04:52:19.680 --> 04:52:23.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Naka-budget na ba tong El Nino preparation natin for the schools?

asr-006090
04:52:23.720 --> 04:52:28.000
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: That's a lot of, a lot of, ano ba yan?

asr-006091
04:52:28.020 --> 04:52:29.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Mga jerry cans o mga...

asr-006092
04:52:29.920 --> 04:52:30.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-006093
04:52:30.900 --> 04:52:35.100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yung rainwater catchment systems, et cetera.

asr-006094
04:52:35.640 --> 04:52:38.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will have to include it in their school MOU, Your Honor.

asr-006095
04:52:38.560 --> 04:52:38.840
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-006096
04:52:39.040 --> 04:52:45.220
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, this next year's MOU, kasama tong mga provisions na ito?

asr-006097
04:52:46.320 --> 04:52:47.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: O ipagkakasya na lang nila?

asr-006098
04:52:47.640 --> 04:52:48.240
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Parang basically...

asr-006099
04:52:48.240 --> 04:52:54.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah, they'll have to work with what we have, Your Honor, to fund this.

asr-006100
04:52:54.240 --> 04:52:57.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi kasama na rin sa'n yung hinihingi nating additional security.

asr-006101
04:52:58.020 --> 04:52:58.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Guards, et cetera.

asr-006102
04:52:59.420 --> 04:53:02.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, these are all things which eat up the MOU.

asr-006103
04:53:03.240 --> 04:53:09.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And then, we're also looking at maybe some upgrading the power systems of schools down the road.

asr-006104
04:53:09.560 --> 04:53:12.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because pag mainit, baka pwede nga ang solar power na lang sila.

asr-006105
04:53:12.680 --> 04:53:14.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Of course, that's a very long-term solution.

asr-006106
04:53:14.940 --> 04:53:16.160
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: For the lights and the fans, no?

asr-006107
04:53:16.200 --> 04:53:19.060
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: I think kaya yung lights and electric fans ng solar, no?

asr-006108
04:53:20.000 --> 04:53:20.440
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Okay.

asr-006109
04:53:20.620 --> 04:53:26.600
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: So, Secretary, maybe just as a suggestion, not really a budget item, but going into next year,

asr-006110
04:53:28.020 --> 04:53:35.080
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: maybe a memo from the executive talking to the teachers and the principals on how to prepare for the El Nino.

asr-006111
04:53:35.320 --> 04:53:36.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, we'll do that.

asr-006112
04:53:36.460 --> 04:53:44.480
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Catchment of water, mga balde, mga jerrycan, or ways to be able to keep water for sanitation.

asr-006113
04:53:44.700 --> 04:53:46.940
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Iba pa yung water for drinking, no?

asr-006114
04:53:46.940 --> 04:53:47.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For drinking, yes, Your Honor.

asr-006115
04:53:47.600 --> 04:53:47.720
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Oo.

asr-006116
04:53:48.400 --> 04:53:55.920
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Kasi kung bibili yung mga skwelahan ng drinking water, that's also going to be a cost in the MOUE.

asr-006117
04:53:56.220 --> 04:53:57.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's right, Your Honor.

asr-006118
04:53:57.020 --> 04:53:57.340
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Yeah.

asr-006119
04:53:58.020 --> 04:53:58.800
Senator Paolo Benigno "Bam" Aquino IV: Please take a look at that.

asr-006120
04:53:58.900 --> 04:53:59.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Will do, Your Honor.

asr-006121
